is more honest than a prisoner, and

5909
08:10:19,494 --> 08:10:20,828
he needed her honest.

5910
08:10:21,399 --> 08:10:27,344
She was fifty-one years old. She had been his chief
financial officer for fifteen years.

5911
08:10:27,364 --> 08:10:33,242
She had a hundred and eighty million dollars, four
homes, and a seat at the table where

5912
08:10:33,262 --> 08:10:34,734
the world was decided.

5913
08:10:35,304 --> 08:10:41,313
And she understood, in a hotel suite in Basel, with
his torn coat on the back of a chair,

5914
08:10:41,333 --> 08:10:47,207
that she was the most thoroughly owned human being
in his entire empire — because every

5915
08:10:47,227 --> 08:10:53,101
single one of the others was owned by something that
had been done to them, and she had

5916
08:10:53,121 --> 08:10:58,047
done it to herself, one reasonable decision
at a time, for fifteen years.

5917
08:11:01,236 --> 08:11:02,634
I want to resign.

5918
08:11:03,155 --> 08:11:04,049
No, you don't.

5919
08:11:24,301 --> 08:11:30,130
The Basel bomb did what Julian Ashcombe had said it
would do. It made Albert Wesker do

5920
08:11:30,150 --> 08:11:33,055
something in public that he
had not chosen.

5921
08:11:33,625 --> 08:11:35,474
It did not do what he had hoped.

5922
08:11:36,044 --> 08:11:41,890
Seventeen billion people had watched a man stand up out
of the smoke and ask whether everyone

5923
08:11:41,910 --> 08:11:47,252
was all right. Most of them had loved him for it.
But in ten capitals, a much smaller

5924
08:11:47,272 --> 08:11:52,740
number of people had watched the same four seconds
and noticed something else entirely:

5925
08:11:52,760 --> 08:11:58,102
that a device of that size, at that distance,
should have killed him, and that he had

5926
08:11:58,122 --> 08:11:59,426
brushed his shoulder.

5927
08:12:01,495 --> 08:12:07,585
Joint Task Force Lantern was formed in November of
twenty forty-two, eight months after

5928
08:12:07,605 --> 08:12:13,765
Basel. Its founding members were the United States,
the United Kingdom, France, Germany,

5929
08:12:13,785 --> 08:12:19,734
Japan, and Canada. Its remit, in the classified
annex that mattered, was to determine

5930
08:12:19,754 --> 08:12:26,265
the nature and capabilities of the individual known as
Albert Wesker, and to develop options.

5931
08:12:26,836 --> 08:12:32,968
It had, from the first week, a serious problem. Nine
of the fourteen intelligence services

5932
08:12:32,988 --> 08:12:38,984
that contributed to it were in countries where
Umbrella was among the largest employers,

5933
08:12:39,004 --> 08:12:45,205
and all fourteen were in countries whose populations
had been vaccinated by Umbrella twice.

5934
08:12:45,774 --> 08:12:51,630
Its senior investigator was a fifty-four-year-old
American civilian contractor named Owen

5935
08:12:51,650 --> 08:12:57,307
Carrick, who had been dismissed from the FBI fifteen
years before for breaking into an

5936
08:12:57,327 --> 08:13:02,985
Umbrella facility, and whose personnel file the
French had insisted on reading in full

5937
08:13:03,005 --> 08:13:08,662
before agreeing to his appointment, and who had
brought with him, into the most secure

5938
08:13:08,682 --> 08:13:13,680
conference room in Brussels, a jam jar
containing fifteen flattened bullets.

5939
08:13:14,250 --> 08:13:19,471
He put it on the table at the first meeting, and
did not explain it, and did not have

5940
08:13:19,491 --> 08:13:19,657
to.

5941
08:13:21,726 --> 08:13:27,889
Samira Haddad joined in the second month, on
secondment from the World Health Organization,

5942
08:13:27,909 --> 08:13:33,051
which believed she was writing a review of
pandemic preparedness governance.

5943
08:13:33,622 --> 08:13:39,931
Ingrid Halvorsen, seventy-four, funded four of the
task force's outside investigators

5944
08:13:39,951 --> 08:13:46,185
through a Norwegian foundation, and never attended
a meeting, and read every report.

5945
08:13:46,755 --> 08:13:52,701
And Julian Ashcombe, who had killed four people in a
Swiss square and would not have another

5946
08:13:52,721 --> 08:13:58,667
peaceful night as long as he lived, was not invited,
and sent them everything he had anyway.

5947
08:14:01,237 --> 08:14:08,172
Lantern spent two years doing what such organisations
do. It mapped. It watched. It compiled.

5948
08:14:08,743 --> 08:14:14,746
It established that Umbrella Life Sciences had, by
twenty forty-four: four hundred and

5949
08:14:14,766 --> 08:14:20,839
eighty thousand direct employees; a market value
larger than the combined stock markets

5950
08:14:20,859 --> 08:14:26,933
of Germany and Japan; the sole manufacturing
capacity for eight medicines without which

5951
08:14:26,953 --> 08:14:33,167
the health systems of forty countries would fail
within a month; a private security force

5952
08:14:33,187 --> 08:14:39,400
of nineteen thousand with its own naval and air
assets; a sovereign-in-practice territory

5953
08:14:39,420 --> 08:14:45,494
in the Atlantic with a hundred and sixty thousand
residents; controlling influence over

5954
08:14:45,514 --> 08:14:51,517
the regulatory regime of the world's pharmaceutical
capital; classified contracts with

5955
08:14:51,537 --> 08:14:57,821
the defence establishments of nine nations; and a
joint research venture with the People's

5956
08:14:57,841 --> 08:14:59,082
Republic of China.

5957
08:14:59,651 --> 08:15:05,462
It established that there were, somewhere,
laboratories that did not appear in any filing.

5958
08:15:05,482 --> 08:15:07,342
It could not establish where.

5959
08:15:07,911 --> 08:15:14,049
And it established, from four separate sources over
two years, that Umbrella possessed

5960
08:15:14,069 --> 08:15:20,350
at least one and possibly several biological assets
of a kind that had no precedent, and

5961
08:15:20,370 --> 08:15:25,433
which two of the sources described,
independently, using the same word.

5962
08:15:26,004 --> 08:15:26,837
Tyrant.

5963
08:15:29,407 --> 08:15:34,264
The raid was authorised by three governments
and executed by none of them.

5964
08:15:34,833 --> 08:15:40,662
It was, on paper, a warrant. A federal magistrate
in Nevada, presented with two years

5965
08:15:40,682 --> 08:15:46,716
of Lantern's work by a Justice Department that had
been fighting internally about it for

5966
08:15:46,736 --> 08:15:52,633
sixteen months, signed a search warrant for the
Ashford Pacific data centre at four in

5967
08:15:52,653 --> 08:15:56,211
the morning on the third of June,
twenty forty-four.

5968
08:15:56,780 --> 08:16:02,994
It was served by two hundred and forty people: an
FBI Hostage Rescue Team, a Department

5969
08:16:03,014 --> 08:16:09,585
of Energy nuclear emergency support team, a CDC
containment unit, and — under an arrangement

5970
08:16:09,605 --> 08:16:15,819
that thirteen lawyers had spent four months
constructing — sixty soldiers from a United

5971
08:16:15,839 --> 08:16:19,545
States Army unit that does not
appear in the budget.

5972
08:16:20,114 --> 08:16:26,020
They came at dawn. They came with helicopters, and
armoured vehicles, and drones, and

5973
08:16:26,040 --> 08:16:31,946
they came, unlike twelve Russians fourteen years
before, entirely in the open, with a

5974
08:16:31,966 --> 08:16:33,898
warrant, on live television.

5975
08:16:34,468 --> 08:16:40,256
That was Carrick's insistence, and it was the
single smartest thing anyone in Lantern

5976
08:16:40,276 --> 08:16:46,269
ever did. He had told them: he can beat you in the
dark. He has done it to me. He cannot

5977
08:16:46,289 --> 08:16:48,045
beat four hundred cameras.

5978
08:16:48,615 --> 08:16:54,341
Umbrella did not resist. The gates were opened for
them. Hale was waiting in the lobby

5979
08:16:54,361 --> 08:17:00,020
with a hand on his chest, in a black uniform, and
said good morning, and offered them

5980
08:17:00,040 --> 08:17:00,487
coffee.

5981
08:17:02,557 --> 08:17:08,523
They went down four levels. They found servers, and
cooling plants, and empty concrete

5982
08:17:08,543 --> 08:17:14,441
rooms. They found a fourth level with bolt holes in
the floor in a rectangle six feet

5983
08:17:14,461 --> 08:17:16,807
by six, and a faint smell of cold.

5984
08:17:17,377 --> 08:17:19,252
They found nothing else at all.

5985
08:17:19,823 --> 08:17:26,048
Umbrella had known about the warrant for nine days,
because a deputy assistant attorney

5986
08:17:26,068 --> 08:17:32,150
general had told a lobbyist, who had told a man on
Umbrella's advisory board, who had

5987
08:17:32,170 --> 08:17:32,868
told Pell.

5988
08:17:35,437 --> 08:17:41,616
What happened at fourteen minutes past six has been
the subject of four national inquiries

5989
08:17:41,636 --> 08:17:47,884
and one international one, and none of them has ever
established, to anyone's satisfaction,

5990
08:17:47,904 --> 08:17:48,986
who fired first.

5991
08:17:49,555 --> 08:17:56,049
There were two hundred and forty federal personnel on
the site. There were, at the perimeter,

5992
08:17:56,069 --> 08:18:02,213
nineteen Umbrella Security Service officers who had
been instructed by Hale, in writing,

5993
08:18:02,233 --> 08:18:05,645
to render every assistance and to
remain unarmed.

5994
08:18:06,215 --> 08:18:11,904
And on the access road, arriving twelve minutes
after the raid began, was a convoy of

5995
08:18:11,924 --> 08:18:17,613
four Umbrella vehicles that no one at Lantern had
known about, carrying an asset that

5996
08:18:17,633 --> 08:18:23,793
had been moved out of the desert complex six days
before and was being brought back, because

5997
08:18:23,813 --> 08:18:27,891
the Director had decided that the world
was ready to see one.

5998
08:18:29,961 --> 08:18:36,530
The firing lasted nineteen seconds. Two federal agents
were wounded, one seriously. Eleven

5999
08:18:36,550 --> 08:18:42,828
Umbrella officers were killed, all of them from the
Shop, all of them standing exactly

6000
08:18:42,848 --> 08:18:46,781
where they had been told to stand,
none of them armed.

6001
08:18:47,352 --> 08:18:50,060
And then the door of the second
vehicle opened.

6002
08:18:54,131 --> 08:18:59,657
The footage from the news helicopter is four minutes
and eleven seconds long, and it is

6003
08:18:59,677 --> 08:19:03,419
the most-watched video in the history
of the human species.

6004
08:19:03,989 --> 08:19:10,298
It shows a nine-foot grey figure stepping down out of
an armoured transport in the Mojave

6005
08:19:10,318 --> 08:19:16,485
Desert at dawn, in front of two hundred and forty
federal officers, on live television,

6006
08:19:16,505 --> 08:19:17,196
in colour.

6007
08:19:17,768 --> 08:19:23,123
It does not attack. That is the thing that every
commentator for the next twenty years

6008
08:19:23,143 --> 08:19:28,623
would come back to. It steps down, and it stands, and
it looks at them — two hundred and

6009
08:19:28,643 --> 08:19:31,999
forty people with rifles — and it
does nothing at all.

6010
08:19:34,567 --> 08:19:40,822
And then a man in a black coat walks out of the dust
behind it, past its right hand, toward

6011
08:19:40,842 --> 08:19:46,683
the federal line, with his hands open and visible,
and stops, and says — to a Hostage

6012
08:19:46,703 --> 08:19:52,613
Rescue Team commander who has aimed at a great many
things in his career and has never

6013
08:19:52,633 --> 08:19:54,751
in his life been so frightened:

6014
08:19:55,440 --> 08:19:59,681
Lower your weapons. Nobody else needs to
die in a car park today.

6015
08:20:01,582 --> 08:20:07,841
My name is Albert Wesker. This is a biological
containment asset, developed under contract

6016
08:20:07,861 --> 08:20:14,190
to the Department of Defense. I have the contract
numbers. I have the clearance. And eleven

6017
08:20:14,210 --> 08:20:17,330
of my unarmed officers are dead
on that road.

6018
08:20:18,729 --> 08:20:20,839
Now. Shall we continue the inspection?

6019
08:20:24,359 --> 08:20:26,399
The world did not sleep for a week.

6020
08:20:26,968 --> 08:20:33,015
The thing in the Mojave had a name within nine
hours, because Umbrella gave it one. Not

6021
08:20:33,035 --> 08:20:39,082
Tyrant. Umbrella's statement — released at nine that
morning, before any government had

6022
08:20:39,102 --> 08:20:45,427
said anything at all — described it as a Class Four
Biological Containment Asset, developed

6023
08:20:45,447 --> 08:20:51,703
under classified contract for the United States
Department of Defense, designed to operate

6024
08:20:51,723 --> 08:20:54,701
in environments lethal to
human responders.

6025
08:20:55,272 --> 08:21:01,228
The Pentagon confirmed the contract that afternoon,
because the contract was real, and

6026
08:21:01,248 --> 08:21:07,272
because Martin Sloane, now sixty-eight and three
years from retirement, had spent seven

6027
08:21:07,292 --> 08:21:10,676
hours on the telephone making
sure that it would.

6028
08:21:11,247 --> 08:21:16,718
What followed was not a scandal about Umbrella. It
was a scandal about the government.

6029
08:21:17,287 --> 08:21:23,697
For six weeks, the story was that the Department of
Defense had secretly funded the development

6030
08:21:23,717 --> 08:21:29,585
of engineered biological soldiers, had lied to
Congress about it, and had then sent two

6031
08:21:29,605 --> 08:21:35,473
hundred and forty federal officers to raid the
facility of the contractor it had itself

6032
08:21:35,493 --> 08:21:41,362
commissioned, killing eleven unarmed men. Two
committee chairs demanded the Secretary's

6033
08:21:41,382 --> 08:21:47,317
resignation. The Justice Department opened an
investigation into the leak that had given

6034
08:21:47,337 --> 08:21:53,138
Umbrella nine days' warning, and found the lobbyist,
and the deputy assistant attorney

6035
08:21:53,158 --> 08:21:57,672
general, and the story became, for another
three weeks, about that.

6036
08:21:58,242 --> 08:22:04,289
Joint Task Force Lantern was not disbanded. It was
worse than disbanded. Two of its six

6037
08:22:04,309 --> 08:22:10,216
member states withdrew. The remaining four were
instructed, by their own governments,

6038
08:22:10,236 --> 08:22:14,120
to restrict their work to legal and
regulatory measures.

6039
08:22:16,690 --> 08:22:22,452
Owen Carrick sat alone in the conference room in
Brussels after the meeting at which he

6040
08:22:22,472 --> 08:22:25,907
was told, and looked at the jam jar
for a long time.

6041
08:22:26,477 --> 08:22:32,154
He had been right for fourteen years. He had finally
got four hundred cameras onto it,

6042
08:22:32,174 --> 08:22:37,254
and the whole world had seen the thing with its
own eyes, in colour, at dawn.

6043
08:22:37,824 --> 08:22:43,442
And the world had watched a nine-foot grey giant
step down out of a truck in front of

6044
08:22:43,462 --> 08:22:49,081
two hundred and forty armed men and stand there
doing nothing while an unarmed man in

6045
08:22:49,101 --> 08:22:54,853
a coat asked them to lower their weapons — and had
concluded, by a margin of about four

6046
08:22:54,873 --> 08:23:00,492
to one in every poll taken in every country that
summer, that the dangerous people in

6047
08:23:00,512 --> 08:23:03,212
that video were the ones with the rifles.

6048
08:23:06,531 --> 08:23:09,348
Assessment. Coalition fractured.

6049
08:23:17,377 --> 08:23:22,980
The eleven dead officers were brought to Arklay and
buried at sea with full honours, in

6050
08:23:23,000 --> 08:23:24,984
front of forty thousand people.

6051
08:23:25,554 --> 08:23:31,057
The Director spoke for two minutes. It was the
shortest and best speech of his life, and

6052
08:23:31,077 --> 08:23:36,517
Tomás Reyes, watching from the production booth,
understood while it was happening that

6053
08:23:36,537 --> 08:23:39,091
it would be studied for a thousand years.

6054
08:23:39,660 --> 08:23:45,425
He did not mention the government. He did not mention
the raid. He named the eleven men,

6055
08:23:45,445 --> 08:23:51,011
one at a time, and said what each of them had done
at their posts that morning, which

6056
08:23:51,031 --> 08:23:54,627
was: exactly what they had been
told, and nothing else.

6057
08:23:55,197 --> 08:23:58,305
Then he said the only sentence
anyone remembers:

6058
08:24:00,495 --> 08:24:05,846
They stood in the open, unarmed, because I asked
them to. I will not ask it again.

6059
08:24:09,366 --> 08:24:15,446
Nineteen governments issued statements of condolence.
Four hundred thousand people applied

6060
08:24:15,466 --> 08:24:19,581
to join the Umbrella Security Service
in the following month.

6061
08:24:20,151 --> 08:24:26,111
And in a room on the fourth floor of an imaginary
brick building, behind a door with no

6062
08:24:26,131 --> 08:24:32,090
name, the old voice said nothing at all — because
for the first time in eighteen years,

6063
08:24:32,110 --> 08:24:35,732
it did not need to explain anything
to the other one.

6064
08:24:36,303 --> 08:24:41,212
They had both understood the same sentence at
the same moment, in the same way.

6065
08:24:57,324 --> 08:25:03,309
The war that decided the twenty-first century had no
front line, no declaration, and —

6066
08:25:03,329 --> 08:25:07,150
for the first twenty-two months — no
casualties at all.

6067
08:25:07,720 --> 08:25:13,834
It began on the eleventh of July, twenty forty-four,
five weeks after the desert, when

6068
08:25:13,854 --> 08:25:19,183
Umbrella Life Sciences announced a review of
its global supply commitments.

6069
08:25:19,753 --> 08:25:25,722
That was the entire announcement. Four hundred and
nineteen words, issued by the corporate

6070
08:25:25,742 --> 08:25:31,578
communications office at seven in the morning, saying
that in light of recent events the

6071
08:25:31,598 --> 08:25:37,301
company was reviewing the security and viability of
its supply arrangements in certain

6072
08:25:37,321 --> 08:25:41,093
jurisdictions, and would update the
market in due course.

6073
08:25:43,164 --> 08:25:47,952
Eighteen medicines. That was what everyone
understood by nine o'clock.

6074
08:25:48,522 --> 08:25:54,719
Aeterna, on which sixty million people depended,
and without which most of them would

6075
08:25:54,739 --> 08:26:01,082
begin to age again within seventeen weeks. The two
Pale Horse boosters, which the World

6076
08:26:01,102 --> 08:26:07,518
Health Organization recommended annually and which
every developed country had built its

6077
08:26:07,538 --> 08:26:14,100
public health policy around. And eight others,
unglamorous and essential — a cardiac drug,

6078
08:26:14,120 --> 08:26:20,390
two antibiotics of last resort, an anticoagulant,
the immunosuppressant used in almost

6079
08:26:20,410 --> 08:26:22,731
every organ transplant on Earth.

6080
08:26:23,300 --> 08:26:28,303
Umbrella had not stopped supplying any of them.
It had said it was reviewing.

6081
08:26:30,493 --> 08:26:32,350
You have not threatened them.

6082
08:26:32,871 --> 08:26:34,430
I have used the word reviewing.

6083
08:26:34,949 --> 08:26:38,365
It is the most violent thing I
have ever heard.

6084
08:26:40,884 --> 08:26:47,765
What followed was not negotiation. It was arithmetic
done in public, by frightened people,

6085
08:26:47,785 --> 08:26:48,532
very fast.

6086
08:26:49,101 --> 08:26:54,738
The health minister of a large European country
calculated that his transplant programme

6087
08:26:54,758 --> 08:27:00,523
had ten weeks of immunosuppressant in the national
stockpile. The Japanese health ministry

6088
08:27:00,543 --> 08:27:05,986
calculated that four hundred thousand of its
citizens over eighty were on Aeterna and

6089
08:27:06,006 --> 08:27:11,578
that the political consequence of interruption was
not survivable. The British National

6090
08:27:11,598 --> 08:27:17,427
Health Service calculated that it could not, under any
circumstances, explain to the public

6091
08:27:17,447 --> 08:27:18,648
why it had run out.

6092
08:27:19,218 --> 08:27:25,290
Nobody had to be told what to do. That was the whole
art of it, and the Director had learned

6093
08:27:25,310 --> 08:27:31,052
it from a deputy assistant secretary at the
Department of Health and Human Services who

6094
08:27:31,072 --> 08:27:36,814
had sat on a report for fifteen months in twenty
thirty because nobody had told him to.

6095
08:27:37,385 --> 08:27:43,412
Within nine days, four of the six governments that
had founded Joint Task Force Lantern

6096
08:27:43,432 --> 08:27:49,320
had privately communicated to Umbrella that they
considered the matters raised by the

6097
08:27:49,340 --> 08:27:51,336
Mojave incident to be closed.

6098
08:27:51,906 --> 08:27:57,901
Within six weeks, three of them had signed long-term
supply agreements which included,

6099
08:27:57,921 --> 08:28:03,916
in an annex, a mutual undertaking regarding
regulatory stability, which meant that any

6100
08:28:03,936 --> 08:28:10,001
future action against Umbrella by any agency of that
government would first be reviewed

6101
08:28:10,021 --> 08:28:11,469
by a joint committee.

6102
08:28:12,039 --> 08:28:18,296
Umbrella resumed normal supply on the twenty-ninth of
August. It had never actually stopped.

6103
08:28:20,866 --> 08:28:26,152
Two of the six did not fold. That is where the
quiet war became a real one.

6104
08:28:26,722 --> 08:28:32,989
The United States and Japan both refused the
regulatory stability annex, and both made

6105
08:28:33,009 --> 08:28:39,350
the same calculation: that Umbrella could not
politically afford to interrupt supply to

6106
08:28:39,370 --> 08:28:43,298
sixty million voters, and that the
threat was a bluff.

6107
08:28:43,868 --> 08:28:48,084
They were right that it was a bluff. They were
wrong about who would be blamed.

6108
08:28:48,656 --> 08:28:54,753
Tomás Reyes had been planning for this since the day
after the desert. He had eight thousand

6109
08:28:54,773 --> 08:28:59,740
people, in nine countries, and a budget that
was not written down anywhere.

6110
08:29:00,309 --> 08:29:06,132
He did not run advertisements. He did not put out
statements. What he did — over nine

6111
08:29:06,152 --> 08:29:12,388
months, in four languages, on every platform there was
— was to make sure that every single

6112
08:29:12,408 --> 08:29:18,575
person in two countries who was worried about their
medicine knew exactly which government

6113
08:29:18,595 --> 08:29:24,486
office to be angry at, and had the address, and had
been shown, gently and repeatedly,

6114
08:29:24,506 --> 08:29:28,130
a video of eleven unarmed men lying
on a desert road.

6115
08:29:28,700 --> 08:29:34,163
It was not disinformation. That was the thing that
made it unanswerable. Every fact in

6116
08:29:34,183 --> 08:29:39,902
it was true. There were eleven unarmed men. There was
a raid. There was a review of supply

6117
08:29:39,922 --> 08:29:45,385
commitments, and it had been triggered by that raid,
and anyone who wanted to know why

6118
08:29:45,405 --> 08:29:50,868
their grandmother's prescription was under review
could read the statement themselves.

6119
08:29:51,438 --> 08:29:58,038
By March of twenty forty-five, the approval rating of
the American administration on healthcare

6120
08:29:58,058 --> 08:30:04,031
was nineteen percent. In Japan, a prime minister who
had been in office for four years

6121
08:30:04,051 --> 08:30:10,373
resigned after losing a vote on an unrelated budget
measure that sixteen of his own party's

6122
08:30:10,393 --> 08:30:12,813
members had used to send a message.

6123
08:30:13,383 --> 08:30:16,648
Both successor governments signed the
annex within a month.

6124
08:30:19,217 --> 08:30:24,857
The narrator has described the quiet war from above,
because that is where it was fought.

6125
08:30:24,877 --> 08:30:30,517
It is necessary to say what it looked like from
underneath, because eleven billion people

6126
08:30:30,537 --> 08:30:35,541
lived through it and almost none of them ever
knew there had been a war at all.

6127
08:30:36,111 --> 08:30:41,929
In a town in Ohio, a pharmacist named Denise Okoro
spent nine weeks telling people that

6128
08:30:41,949 --> 08:30:47,900
she did not know. She did not know whether the next
shipment was coming. She did not know

6129
08:30:47,920 --> 08:30:53,670
whether the review would end. She had four hundred
regular patients on Aeterna and she

6130
08:30:53,690 --> 08:30:59,441
had, at the worst of it, eleven days of stock, and
she was forty-six years old and she

6131
08:30:59,461 --> 08:31:05,144
cried in the back room twice a day for nine weeks
and then went out and told the next

6132
08:31:05,164 --> 08:31:08,566
person in the queue, calmly, that
she did not know.

6133
08:31:09,135 --> 08:31:15,196
Nobody died. That is the crucial fact, and the
Directorate's defenders have leaned on

6134
08:31:15,216 --> 08:31:21,276
it for two centuries, and it is true. Supply was
never actually interrupted anywhere.

6135
08:31:21,296 --> 08:31:24,351
Not one dose was withheld from
one patient.

6136
08:31:24,923 --> 08:31:30,122
What was withheld was certainty, for nine weeks,
from four hundred million people who

6137
08:31:30,142 --> 08:31:35,526
had organised their lives around it. And at the end
of the nine weeks the certainty came

6138
08:31:35,546 --> 08:31:40,745
back, and the people who had taken it away were the
same people who gave it back, and

6139
08:31:40,765 --> 08:31:46,149
almost everybody in the world was so relieved that
they never worked out that those were

6140
08:31:46,169 --> 08:31:47,131
the same people.

6141
08:31:49,202 --> 08:31:54,844
Denise Okoro worked that out. She worked it out in
about the fourth week, standing in

6142
08:31:54,864 --> 08:31:55,777
her back room.

6143
08:31:56,347 --> 08:32:02,082
She wrote to her congressman about it, and got a
thoughtful reply. She wrote to a newspaper,

6144
08:32:02,102 --> 08:32:07,586
and it was printed, in a section for letters. She
told her husband, who agreed with her.

6145
08:32:07,606 --> 08:32:13,090
And then the shipments resumed, and her patients were
fine, and four years later her own

6146
08:32:13,110 --> 08:32:18,407
mother went on Aeterna and walked her granddaughter
to school, and Denise Okoro never

6147
08:32:18,427 --> 08:32:20,220
mentioned it again to anyone.

6148
08:32:20,791 --> 08:32:26,221
There is no conspiracy in that. Nobody silenced her.
She simply lived in a world where

6149
08:32:26,241 --> 08:32:31,798
being right about the shape of a thing changed
nothing at all about the thing, and after

6150
08:32:31,818 --> 08:32:36,805
a while she stopped spending her evenings on it,
because she had a shop to run.

6151
08:32:39,375 --> 08:32:45,135
That happened four hundred million times. That is the
whole mechanism. It has no villain

6152
08:32:45,155 --> 08:32:50,916
in it anywhere except at the very top, and at the
very top it was a man in an office who

6153
08:32:50,936 --> 08:32:57,091
never once had to give an instruction, because he had
only ever had to use the word reviewing.

6154
08:33:00,162 --> 08:33:05,756
There was fighting. It is largely forgotten, because
it happened in places that do not

6155
08:33:05,776 --> 08:33:06,801
photograph well.

6156
08:33:07,371 --> 08:33:13,633
In April of twenty forty-five, over thirteen days,
the networks of Umbrella Life Sciences

6157
08:33:13,653 --> 08:33:19,774
were attacked more comprehensively than any private
organisation in history. Four state

6158
08:33:19,794 --> 08:33:26,198
actors were involved, at least two of them working
together, and the attacks were extremely

6159
08:33:26,218 --> 08:33:26,551
good.

6160
08:33:27,121 --> 08:33:33,024
They failed. Not because Umbrella's defences were
better — though they were — but because

6161
08:33:33,044 --> 08:33:39,014
Sebastian Crane had spent a decade building something
that no state had: a security system

6162
08:33:39,034 --> 08:33:44,672
that modelled its attackers the way Oracle had once
modelled companies, and that had,

6163
08:33:44,692 --> 08:33:48,731
on the second day, begun to predict
where they would go next.

6164
08:33:49,302 --> 08:33:55,307
Crane was fifty-one. He had taken the longevity
therapy at forty-four, and the other thing

6165
08:33:55,327 --> 08:34:01,064
at forty-eight. He worked eighteen hours a day in a
windowless room on the second ring

6166
08:34:01,084 --> 08:34:06,755
of Arklay, and he had not been off the Territory in
three years, and he was, by every

6167
08:34:06,775 --> 08:34:11,843
account of everyone who knew him, happier than
he had ever been in his life.

6168
08:34:12,414 --> 08:34:18,067
On the ninth day, he found the attackers' own
command network and did not destroy it.

6169
08:34:18,087 --> 08:34:23,875
He watched it for thirty-one hours, and mapped it,
and then sent the map — anonymously,

6170
08:34:23,895 --> 08:34:30,083
through four intermediaries — to the intelligence
service of a country that was not involved,

6171
08:34:30,103 --> 08:34:31,752
and let them do the rest.

6172
08:34:32,322 --> 08:34:36,744
Two of the four state actors spent the
following year fighting each other.

6173
08:34:39,313 --> 08:34:41,340
And then cities began to choose.

6174
08:34:41,910 --> 08:34:47,970
Not countries, at first. Cities, and then regions,
and then two small states whose names

6175
08:34:47,990 --> 08:34:51,286
are now taught to schoolchildren
on nine worlds.

6176
08:34:51,856 --> 08:34:57,508
It began in a country where it should not have
begun: a middle-income nation of seven

6177
08:34:57,528 --> 08:35:03,445
million people, with a functioning democracy, a
health system under strain, and a coastal

6178
08:35:03,465 --> 08:35:09,116
province that had been devastated by a storm in
twenty forty-three and never rebuilt.

6179
08:35:09,687 --> 08:35:15,365
Umbrella's foundation had been in that province for
nine years. It ran forty-one clinics

6180
08:35:15,385 --> 08:35:21,192
there. After the storm it had rebuilt the hospital in
the provincial capital in twenty-two

6181
08:35:21,212 --> 08:35:26,696
weeks, which was nine years faster than the
national government had rebuilt anything,

6182
08:35:26,716 --> 08:35:32,524
and it had then rebuilt the schools, and the water
system, and eventually, because someone

6183
08:35:32,544 --> 08:35:33,690
had to, the roads.

6184
08:35:34,260 --> 08:35:40,678
By twenty forty-five the province's governor had been
to Arklay four times. Her provincial

6185
08:35:40,698 --> 08:35:46,759
assembly passed, in September of that year, a
resolution requesting that the national

6186
08:35:46,779 --> 08:35:52,840
government negotiate a framework of association
with Umbrella Life Sciences, covering

6187
08:35:52,860 --> 08:35:56,060
health, education,
infrastructure, and water.

6188
08:35:56,630 --> 08:36:03,710
The national government refused. The province held a
referendum anyway, which was unconstitutional,

6189
08:36:03,730 --> 08:36:06,650
and which passed with eighty-one percent.

6190
08:36:07,221 --> 08:36:13,100
There was a constitutional crisis, and a general
strike, and nineteen days in which soldiers

6191
08:36:13,120 --> 08:36:18,679
were deployed to the provincial capital and did
nothing, because the soldiers were from

6192
08:36:18,699 --> 08:36:22,462
that province and their own children
went to those schools.

6193
08:36:23,031 --> 08:36:29,669
The framework of association was signed in January of
twenty forty-six. It did not change

6194
08:36:29,689 --> 08:36:36,028
the province's flag, or its passports, or its
membership of the United Nations, which

6195
08:36:36,048 --> 08:36:39,918
it did not have. It changed who
built the hospitals.

6196
08:36:43,239 --> 08:36:45,120
Territory. Accession.

6197
08:36:50,424 --> 08:36:53,682
Four million people. The System
counted them all.

6198
08:36:55,871 --> 08:36:57,651
Not one soldier.

6199
08:36:58,172 --> 08:36:58,914
Not one.

6200
08:36:59,433 --> 08:37:05,173
I took the Rhineland with three battalions and I
could not sleep for a week. You have

6201
08:37:05,193 --> 08:37:07,679
taken a province with a water system.

6202
08:37:08,199 --> 08:37:12,596
I've taken the first one with a water system.
The others will be cheaper.

6203
08:37:15,116 --> 08:37:20,568
There were eighteen more frameworks of association
in the following four years. Two of

6204
08:37:20,588 --> 08:37:22,286
them were entire countries.

6205
08:37:22,856 --> 08:37:28,469
Catherine Adeyemi signed the financial annex to
every one of them. She was fifty-five,

6206
08:37:28,489 --> 08:37:34,495
and then fifty-six, and then fifty-seven. She had
stopped sending reports to Julian Ashcombe

6207
08:37:34,515 --> 08:37:40,651
in twenty forty-four — not because she had been told to,
but because he had stopped answering,

6208
08:37:40,671 --> 08:37:46,219
and because she had come to understand that there
was no longer anywhere to send them

6209
08:37:46,239 --> 08:37:47,135
that mattered.

6210
08:37:47,706 --> 08:37:53,743
She did her job extremely well. Umbrella's accounts,
in a world where almost nothing was

6211
08:37:53,763 --> 08:38:00,007
audited anymore, remained the most honest set of books
on the planet, because she insisted,

6212
08:38:00,027 --> 08:38:04,069
and because she was the only person
alive who could insist.

6213
08:38:04,639 --> 08:38:10,535
She kept a photograph on her desk. It was not of her
family. It was a picture that Dana

6214
08:38:10,555 --> 08:38:16,520
Whitfield had given her, years before, of a
four-storey brick building on the south bank

6215
08:38:16,540 --> 08:38:22,709
of the Christina River, with a faded blue sign above
the door, taken in twenty twenty-five.

6216
08:38:23,279 --> 08:38:29,471
People assumed it was sentiment about the company's
origins. Tomás's department used it

6217
08:38:29,491 --> 08:38:30,543
once in a film.

6218
08:38:31,111 --> 08:38:36,474
It was not sentiment. It was a control. She looked at
it, every morning, to remind herself

6219
08:38:36,494 --> 08:38:41,677
what the thing she worked for had looked like when
it was small enough to be understood

6220
08:38:41,697 --> 08:38:46,282
— so that she would notice, when she had
stopped being able to understand it.

6221
08:39:05,000 --> 08:39:10,656
By the winter of twenty forty-six, the President of
the United States had two problems,

6222
08:39:10,676 --> 08:39:12,678
and they were the same problem.

6223
08:39:13,248 --> 08:39:19,064
The first was that forty-one million Americans took a
medicine that only one company made,

6224
08:39:19,084 --> 08:39:24,834
and that ninety-one percent of them, in every poll
her office ran, said they trusted that

6225
08:39:24,854 --> 08:39:30,670
company more than they trusted their government. The
second was that she had been elected,

6226
08:39:30,690 --> 08:39:34,689
eighteen months before, on a promise to
do something about it.

6227
08:39:35,259 --> 08:39:40,890
She was sixty-three. She had been a governor, and a
prosecutor before that, and she was

6228
08:39:40,910 --> 08:39:46,476
nobody's fool, and she had spent her first year
discovering, department by department,

6229
08:39:46,496 --> 08:39:51,931
exactly how deep the roots had gone while everyone
was arguing about something else.

6230
08:39:54,002 --> 08:40:00,274
In January, her national security adviser had given
her a document that four people had

6231
08:40:00,294 --> 08:40:06,710
read. It was an assessment of what would happen if
the United States government attempted

6232
08:40:06,730 --> 08:40:11,917
to seize Umbrella Life Sciences' domestic
assets under emergency powers.

6233
08:40:12,487 --> 08:40:18,411
The conclusion was on the first page, in one
sentence: the United States does not possess

6234
08:40:18,431 --> 08:40:24,422
the capacity to do this without causing the deaths of
a number of its own citizens greater

6235
08:40:24,442 --> 08:40:27,962
than any war it has fought since
eighteen sixty-five.

6236
08:40:30,532 --> 08:40:34,557
Owen Carrick was fifty-eight when he
finally got into the building.

6237
08:40:35,128 --> 08:40:41,331
It had taken him sixteen years. He had shown the
bullets to four journalists, two members

6238
08:40:41,351 --> 08:40:47,555
of Congress, a Pentagon official, and a priest, and
then to a Norwegian heiress, and then

6239
08:40:47,575 --> 08:40:53,778
to a task force that had been dismantled around him.
And in February of twenty forty-six,

6240
08:40:53,798 --> 08:40:59,862
a deputy national security adviser who had read
every Lantern report and had a daughter

6241
08:40:59,882 --> 08:41:06,086
on Aeterna asked him to come in on a Tuesday morning
and tell the President of the United

6242
08:41:06,106 --> 08:41:08,324
States what he thought was true.

6243
08:41:08,894 --> 08:41:14,600
He had forty minutes. He had prepared for eleven
days. He did not bring the jam jar; they

6244
08:41:14,620 --> 08:41:17,366
would not let him through the
gate with it.

6245
08:41:18,056 --> 08:41:23,254
Ma'am, I'm going to say four things that sound
insane, and then I'm going to give you

6246
08:41:23,274 --> 08:41:26,752
the evidence for each one, and then
you can throw me out.

6247
08:41:27,273 --> 08:41:33,011
He said them. He was very clear, and very calm, and
he had rehearsed it so many times

6248
08:41:33,031 --> 08:41:34,976
that he did not stumble once.

6249
08:41:35,545 --> 08:41:41,807
One: Albert Wesker was not a human being, in the
ordinary sense. Two: he had been in possession

6250
08:41:41,827 --> 08:41:48,154
of capabilities that no institution on Earth could
account for since at least twenty twenty-six.

6251
08:41:48,174 --> 08:41:53,972
Three: everything Umbrella had built — the medicines,
the Foundation, the Territory, the

6252
08:41:53,992 --> 08:41:59,790
frameworks of association — was not the goal, but the
method. And four: he intended, and

6253
08:41:59,810 --> 08:42:01,708
had always intended, to rule.

6254
08:42:03,898 --> 08:42:07,110
Mister Carrick. Do you know what the worst
part of this briefing is?

6255
08:42:07,631 --> 08:42:08,345
Ma'am?

6256
08:42:08,864 --> 08:42:10,487
That I already believe you.

6257
08:42:12,887 --> 08:42:17,675
I've had this conversation four times in fourteen
months, with four different people,

6258
08:42:17,695 --> 08:42:22,824
each of whom thought they were the first. The Bureau
believes you. Half of Langley believes

6259
08:42:22,844 --> 08:42:27,859
you. My science adviser believes you and can't say
so, because the moment she does, she's

6260
08:42:27,879 --> 08:42:28,311
a crank.

6261
08:42:28,713 --> 08:42:29,951
And it doesn't matter.

6262
08:42:30,471 --> 08:42:31,455
Why not?

6263
08:42:31,977 --> 08:42:36,709
Because I asked the Joint Chiefs to give me options
in January, and they gave me a page

6264
08:42:36,729 --> 08:42:41,515
that says a hundred and twenty thousand Americans die
in the first eleven weeks. Because

6265
08:42:41,535 --> 08:42:46,213
forty-one million people would rather have their
medicine than their sovereignty and I

6266
08:42:46,233 --> 08:42:50,965
cannot say that out loud. Because he has never
broken a law in this country that we can

6267
08:42:50,985 --> 08:42:55,772
prove, and because he owns the only factory on Earth
that makes eight things my citizens

6268
08:42:55,792 --> 08:42:56,810
need to stay alive.

6269
08:42:58,709 --> 08:43:03,522
You caught him, Mister Carrick. Sixteen years ago,
on a dashcam, in a parking lot. You

6270
08:43:03,542 --> 08:43:08,636
were right about all of it, and nobody believed you,
and by the time we did, it was already

6271
08:43:08,656 --> 08:43:09,703
too late to matter.

6272
08:43:12,223 --> 08:43:18,220
Owen Carrick sat in the Oval Office and understood,
at last, the thing that he had spent

6273
08:43:18,239 --> 08:43:21,227
his whole adult life refusing
to understand.

6274
08:43:21,797 --> 08:43:27,309
He had always believed that the problem was that
nobody knew. That if he could only get

6275
08:43:27,329 --> 08:43:32,714
the evidence in front of the right person, the
machinery of the world would turn, and

6276
08:43:32,734 --> 08:43:34,239
something would be done.

6277
08:43:34,809 --> 08:43:39,290
The machinery knew. It had known for years.
It simply could not move.

6278
08:43:42,361 --> 08:43:48,084
The Director came to Washington eleven days later,
at the President's invitation, and

6279
08:43:48,104 --> 08:43:49,030
he came alone.

6280
08:43:49,600 --> 08:43:55,044
That was a decision, and it was the whole meeting.
He had a security force of nineteen

6281
08:43:55,064 --> 08:44:00,762
thousand, a private air fleet, and a personal risk
profile that four intelligence services

6282
08:44:00,782 --> 08:44:06,480
had assessed as the highest of any individual alive.
He arrived in one car, with a driver,

6283
08:44:06,500 --> 08:44:12,262
and walked through the North Portico with his hands in
his coat pockets, and let the Secret

6284
08:44:12,282 --> 08:44:15,692
Service search him, and stood there
while they did it.

6285
08:44:16,263 --> 08:44:22,485
They met alone. No aides, no notetaker, no recording
— which was itself unprecedented,

6286
08:44:22,505 --> 08:44:27,349
and which her chief of staff argued
against for two days, and lost.

6287
08:44:28,039 --> 08:44:33,111
I'll be direct, Doctor Wesker. I've been advised
that my government cannot compel you

6288
08:44:33,131 --> 08:44:38,262
to do anything. I've also been advised that any
attempt to try would kill a great many

6289
08:44:38,282 --> 08:44:41,438
of my citizens. I don't enjoy being
in that position.

6290
08:44:41,958 --> 08:44:43,187
No. I wouldn't either.

6291
08:44:43,706 --> 08:44:48,487
So I'm going to ask you a question, and I'd like an
honest answer, and I have nothing

6292
08:44:48,506 --> 08:44:50,407
to trade for it. What do you want?

6293
08:44:52,926 --> 08:44:58,644
He took off his sunglasses. He did that, in this
world, perhaps four times a year, and

6294
08:44:58,664 --> 08:45:01,046
every single time it was a decision.

6295
08:45:01,736 --> 08:45:05,791
I want the same thing you do, Madam
President. I want it to work.

6296
08:45:06,311 --> 08:45:07,568
Want what to work?

6297
08:45:08,088 --> 08:45:13,460
All of it. The species. You've been in office for
eighteen months. You've seen the actual

6298
08:45:13,480 --> 08:45:18,671
numbers — the water tables, the heat, the debt, the
demographics, the four wars nobody

6299
08:45:18,691 --> 08:45:24,124
can stop. You know what your grandchildren's century
looks like on the current trajectory.

6300
08:45:24,144 --> 08:45:29,274
Everyone in this building knows. And every one of
you has worked out, privately, that

6301
08:45:29,294 --> 08:45:34,849
your system cannot fix it, because your system is
designed to produce a new set of temporary

6302
08:45:34,869 --> 08:45:40,060
people every four years, each of whom is punished
for doing anything that takes longer

6303
08:45:40,080 --> 08:45:40,666
than that.

6304
08:45:42,066 --> 08:45:46,630
I am not a temporary person. That is the
entire difference between us.

6305
08:45:48,650 --> 08:45:50,145
And what does that make you?

6306
08:45:50,664 --> 08:45:51,433
Patient.

6307
08:45:53,953 --> 08:45:59,275
She did not say anything for a while. The fire
made the only noise in the room.

6308
08:45:59,965 --> 08:46:04,785
My mother is eighty-nine. She's been on Aeterna
for nine years. She gardens.

6309
08:46:05,306 --> 08:46:05,990
I know.

6310
08:46:06,510 --> 08:46:07,749
Of course you do.

6311
08:46:09,148 --> 08:46:13,713
When you take this country — and I've read enough to
know that you intend to, and that

6312
08:46:13,733 --> 08:46:18,298
you'll do it with frameworks and water systems and
not with soldiers — how long do you

6313
08:46:18,318 --> 08:46:19,097
think it takes?

6314
08:46:21,117 --> 08:46:26,578
If I am careless? Forty years. If I am not? You won't be
able to point at the day it happened.

6315
08:46:29,100 --> 08:46:32,532
That's the most honest thing anyone has
said to me in this office.

6316
08:46:33,052 --> 08:46:38,502
It's the most honest thing anyone will say to you
in this office. That's not a boast.

6317
08:46:38,522 --> 08:46:40,239
It's the nature of the job.

6318
08:46:43,260 --> 08:46:47,519
Owen Carrick went home and did not get out
of the chair for two days.

6319
08:46:48,090 --> 08:46:53,851
He was fifty-eight. He had been an FBI agent for
seventeen years and a man who knew for

6320
08:46:53,871 --> 08:47:00,031
sixteen. He had lost his badge, his pension, his
marriage, and eleven years of two daughters'

6321
08:47:00,051 --> 08:47:05,945
childhoods, which was the loss that actually mattered
and which he had never once allowed

6322
08:47:05,965 --> 08:47:07,142
himself to add up.

6323
08:47:07,712 --> 08:47:14,001
Laura had remarried. She had told him about it
kindly, on the phone, in twenty forty-one.

6324
08:47:14,021 --> 08:47:20,168
His elder daughter was a doctor in Portland. She had
taken Aeterna, as a precaution, at

6325
08:47:20,188 --> 08:47:23,713
twenty-nine, because everyone in
her hospital did.

6326
08:47:25,782 --> 08:47:28,366
He looked at the jam jar for a long time.

6327
08:47:28,936 --> 08:47:35,709
And he found — this is the part he never told anyone,
not Haddad, not Halvorsen, not Hannah

6328
08:47:35,729 --> 08:47:38,845
Price — that what he felt was not despair.

6329
08:47:39,415 --> 08:47:40,610
It was relief.

6330
08:47:41,181 --> 08:47:46,795
For sixteen years he had believed that he was the
only thing standing between the world

6331
08:47:46,815 --> 08:47:52,429
and Albert Wesker. It had been the worst kind of
loneliness, and the most complete kind

6332
08:47:52,449 --> 08:47:57,933
of purpose, and it had eaten his entire life. And
in an office in Washington, a woman

6333
08:47:57,953 --> 08:48:03,438
with a nuclear arsenal had told him: we know, we
all know, and there is nothing to be

6334
08:48:03,458 --> 08:48:03,761
done.

6335
08:48:04,330 --> 08:48:10,180
He was not the only thing standing anymore. He was
not standing at all. Nobody was.

6336
08:48:12,749 --> 08:48:18,249
On the third morning he got up, and showered, and
packed a bag, and drove to Portland,

6337
08:48:18,269 --> 08:48:23,833
Oregon, and knocked on his daughter's door on a
Saturday morning without calling ahead.

6338
08:48:24,402 --> 08:48:29,889
She let him in. It took eleven months before she
stopped being angry with him and four

6339
08:48:29,909 --> 08:48:35,460
years before they could talk about anything that
mattered, and he had both. Aeterna had

6340
08:48:35,480 --> 08:48:41,351
given him thirty more years, and he had started taking
it in twenty forty-one, like everyone

6341
08:48:41,371 --> 08:48:43,401
else, because everyone else did.

6342
08:48:43,970 --> 08:48:50,349
That is how Owen Carrick's war ended. Not in a
courtroom, or a desert, or a corridor under

6343
08:48:50,369 --> 08:48:56,535
a brick building. In a kitchen in Portland, with a
daughter who did not want to talk to

6344
08:48:56,555 --> 08:49:00,161
him, and a jam jar left on a shelf
in Pennsylvania.

6345
08:49:02,729 --> 08:49:08,311
He lived a long time. He saw all of it. He saw the
Accord, and the ships, and the things

6346
08:49:08,331 --> 08:49:13,976
that came back from the dark with Umbrella's mark on
them, and he told his grandchildren,

6347
08:49:13,996 --> 08:49:19,641
when they were old enough, that he had once shot a
man fifteen times and been handed back

6348
08:49:19,661 --> 08:49:20,405
the bullets.

6349
08:49:20,975 --> 08:49:23,345
They thought it was a story. He let them.

6350
08:49:26,916 --> 08:49:31,764
On the flight back to Arklay, the Director sat
in the dark and did not work.

6351
08:49:32,454 --> 08:49:34,034
She capitulated.

6352
08:49:34,553 --> 08:49:40,101
She didn't. She surveyed the ground, found it
indefensible, and told me so to my face.

6353
08:49:40,121 --> 08:49:45,733
That isn't capitulation. That's the first competent
thing any government has done about

6354
08:49:45,753 --> 08:49:46,964
us in twenty years.

6355
08:49:47,484 --> 08:49:48,830
You liked her.

6356
08:49:49,350 --> 08:49:51,228
I respected her. It's rarer.

6357
08:49:53,249 --> 08:49:59,045
Do you remember what you said to me? In the car, in
the rain, in the first week. You said:

6358
08:49:59,065 --> 08:50:01,436
you lost because they saw you coming.

6359
08:50:01,955 --> 08:50:02,811
I remember.

6360
08:50:03,330 --> 08:50:09,110
They see you coming. That woman sees you coming.
The policeman saw you coming sixteen

6361
08:50:09,130 --> 08:50:14,978
years ago, in four frames of a dashboard camera. The
Chinese woman has seen you coming

6362
08:50:14,998 --> 08:50:19,140
since she listened to your silences.
They all see you coming.

6363
08:50:20,540 --> 08:50:26,344
And they cannot do anything about it. Which means it
was never about being seen at all.

6364
08:50:28,864 --> 08:50:34,794
The Wesker half of the mind sat with that for a
long time, over the dark Atlantic, at

6365
08:50:34,814 --> 08:50:36,474
forty-one thousand feet.

6366
08:50:37,043 --> 08:50:42,484
It was, he realised, the first thing the old voice
had ever taught him that he had not

6367
08:50:42,504 --> 08:50:43,373
already known.

6368
08:50:43,942 --> 08:50:49,239
It had never been about being unseen. Hiding had
only ever been a way of buying time.

6369
08:50:49,259 --> 08:50:54,869
The thing that actually mattered — the thing he had
been building for twenty years without

6370
08:50:54,889 --> 08:51:00,498
ever quite saying it to himself — was to become
necessary. And a necessary thing can stand

6371
08:51:00,518 --> 08:51:06,003
in a cathedral square in broad daylight, in front of
four hundred cameras, and brush the

6372
08:51:06,023 --> 08:51:09,819
dust off its shoulder, and ask whether
everyone is all right.

6373
08:51:12,008 --> 08:51:12,608
Huh.

6374
08:51:13,128 --> 08:51:13,994
Yes.

6375
08:51:16,144 --> 08:51:20,924
Integration. Host coherence,
ninety-seven percent.

6376
08:51:24,514 --> 08:51:25,395
Zero.

6377
08:51:25,965 --> 08:51:31,685
He looked at that number for a long time, in the dark,
with the ocean going past underneath.

6378
08:51:32,254 --> 08:51:37,500
In the first year there had been four hundred
arguments. Last year there had been two.

6379
08:51:37,520 --> 08:51:42,765
This year there had been none at all — and he had
not noticed, which was the part that

6380
08:51:59,084 --> 08:52:03,684
The last government on Earth that could have
stopped him invited him to dinner.

6381
08:52:04,253 --> 08:52:09,589
It had taken two years to arrange, through four
intermediaries, and the terms had been

6382
08:52:09,609 --> 08:52:15,194
negotiated with the seriousness of an arms control
treaty. He would come without security.

6383
08:52:15,214 --> 08:52:20,736
There would be no announcement, before or after.
There would be no photographs. And there

6384
08:52:20,756 --> 08:52:26,029
would be one other person at the table, who would
not be named in any record, because

6385
08:52:26,049 --> 08:52:31,510
she did not officially exist in any capacity that
would permit her to sit at that table.

6386
08:52:32,080 --> 08:52:37,780
Wen Shulan was seventy-one. She had been a deputy
minister of state security for eleven

6387
08:52:37,800 --> 08:52:43,368
years and then something without a title for eight
more, and she had spent twenty-two

6388
08:52:43,388 --> 08:52:48,364
years, on and off, reading everything there was
to read about Albert Wesker.

6389
08:52:48,934 --> 08:52:53,762
She had been right about him before anyone else on
Earth, and she had never once been

6390
08:52:53,782 --> 08:52:57,527
able to say so in a sentence that would
not have ended her career.

6391
08:52:59,596 --> 08:53:05,520
The third person at the table was a member of the
Politburo Standing Committee whose name

6392
08:53:05,540 --> 08:53:11,464
does not matter to this story, and who said perhaps
forty words all evening, and listened

6393
08:53:11,484 --> 08:53:13,134
to every one of the rest.

6394
08:53:15,324 --> 08:53:17,430
You have taken eleven countries.

6395
08:53:17,950 --> 08:53:24,135
Association agreements with two states and nine
provinces. Nobody's flag has changed.

6396
08:53:24,655 --> 08:53:30,044
Doctor Wesker. We are three people in a room with no
recording. Let us not waste the evening.

6397
08:53:31,563 --> 08:53:34,979
Fourteen, then. There are three more that
haven't been announced.

6398
08:53:36,998 --> 08:53:43,053
The Standing Committee member did not look up from his
soup. Wen Shulan smiled — the second

6399
08:53:43,073 --> 08:53:46,792
smile anyone at the Ministry had ever
recorded from her.

6400
08:53:47,482 --> 08:53:48,507
Thank you.

6401
08:53:51,027 --> 08:53:56,347
What followed was the most consequential
conversation of the twenty-first century, and

6402
08:53:56,367 --> 08:53:57,527
the least dramatic.

6403
08:53:58,096 --> 08:54:04,349
There was no threat. Both sides had worked out,
years before, exactly what threats were

6404
08:54:04,369 --> 08:54:10,695
available and exactly why none of them worked. China
could not embargo Umbrella; a fifth

6405
08:54:10,715 --> 08:54:16,967
of its own pharmaceutical supply and most of its
vaccine capacity ran through the joint

6406
08:54:16,987 --> 08:54:23,673
venture in Singapore. Umbrella could not coerce China;
China made forty percent of everything

6407
08:54:23,693 --> 08:54:30,162
Umbrella's factories assembled, and had done for a
generation, and had spent fifteen years

6408
08:54:30,182 --> 08:54:33,118
quietly ensuring that this remained true.

6409
08:54:33,688 --> 08:54:39,621
They were not enemies. They were the only two
structures left on Earth of comparable weight,

6410
08:54:39,641 --> 08:54:45,185
and they both knew it, and the entire evening was
about establishing, precisely, where

6411
08:54:45,205 --> 08:54:46,026
the line ran.

6412
08:54:48,217 --> 08:54:50,290
You will not take our provinces.

6413
08:54:50,811 --> 08:54:51,430
No.

6414
08:54:51,950 --> 08:54:55,168
You will not take the provinces of our
neighbours who look to us.

6415
08:54:55,688 --> 08:54:57,581
That's a longer list than the first one.

6416
08:54:58,102 --> 08:54:59,172
It is.

6417
08:55:00,692 --> 08:55:06,720
Then let's write it down. Not as a treaty — neither
of us can sign a treaty. As a map,

6418
08:55:06,740 --> 08:55:11,221
with names on it, which neither of us
will ever show to anybody.

6419
08:55:13,241 --> 08:55:19,212
They spent four hours on the map. It was the only
physical object produced that evening,

6420
08:55:19,232 --> 08:55:25,067
and there were two copies, and both of them still
exist, and one of them is in a vault

6421
08:55:25,087 --> 08:55:29,220
under a mountain outside Beijing, and
the other is on Arklay.

6422
08:55:29,789 --> 08:55:36,085
It divided the surface of the Earth into three parts:
what was China's, what was Umbrella's,

6423
08:55:36,105 --> 08:55:40,616
and what was neither — which, in twenty
forty-six, was most of it.

6424
08:55:43,186 --> 08:55:49,114
It held for nineteen years. That is a very long
time, for a line drawn on a map by two

6425
08:55:49,134 --> 08:55:51,812
people who had no authority to draw it.

6426
08:55:53,882 --> 08:55:59,737
At eleven o'clock the Standing Committee member
thanked them both, and left, and did not

6427
08:55:59,757 --> 08:56:02,341
come back. That had also been arranged.

6428
08:56:02,911 --> 08:56:05,411
Wen Shulan poured the last of the tea.

6429
08:56:06,101 --> 08:56:08,743
May I ask you something that is
not business?

6430
08:56:09,263 --> 08:56:10,176
You've earned one.

6431
08:56:10,696 --> 08:56:16,178
Twenty-two years ago I watched a recording of you
sitting in silence on an American television

6432
08:56:16,198 --> 08:56:21,154
programme, and I recognised the rhythm of it. I
have never been able to say to anyone

6433
08:56:21,174 --> 08:56:26,130
what I recognised, because it is not sayable. But I
would like to say it once, aloud,

6434
08:56:26,150 --> 08:56:28,648
to you, and then I will never
say it again.

6435
08:56:31,047 --> 08:56:35,844
My grandfather was in Nanjing in nineteen
thirty-seven. He was nine years old. He did

6436
08:56:35,864 --> 08:56:40,718
not talk about it for fifty years, and then he
talked about it for one evening, when I

6437
08:56:40,738 --> 08:56:44,061
was a grown woman, and then he never
talked about it again.

6438
08:56:45,960 --> 08:56:50,789
When I listen to you speak, Doctor Wesker, I hear
the cadence of the men who did that

6439
08:56:50,809 --> 08:56:55,638
to my grandfather's city. Not the language. The
shape. The pause before the important

6440
08:56:55,658 --> 08:56:59,688
word. The way a sentence is built so that a
crowd will breathe with it.

6441
08:57:01,588 --> 08:57:06,376
I do not know what you are. I have stopped trying
to know. But I know that shape, and

6442
08:57:06,396 --> 08:57:11,409
I want you to understand that one person on this
planet hears it every time you open your

6443
08:57:11,429 --> 08:57:11,748
mouth.

6444
08:57:14,768 --> 08:57:17,582
In the quiet of one skull, nothing moved.

6445
08:57:18,152 --> 08:57:24,396
The Adolf half of the mind — which had spent twenty
years being described, in a hundred

6446
08:57:24,416 --> 08:57:30,876
ways, by people who had no idea it was there — heard
itself identified, accurately, across

6447
08:57:30,896 --> 08:57:34,188
a dinner table, by an old woman
with a teapot.

6448
08:57:34,758 --> 08:57:41,062
And the Wesker half felt the thing it had felt exactly
twice before: at a dinner in Philadelphia,

6449
08:57:41,082 --> 08:57:46,670
when a journalist had asked about Control Seven, and
in a doorway, on the first night,

6450
08:57:46,690 --> 08:57:50,126
when an old security guard had said
different animal.

6451
08:57:52,316 --> 08:57:56,221
And knowing that, you've just spent four
hours drawing a map with me.

6452
08:57:56,741 --> 08:57:57,622
Yes.

6453
08:57:58,142 --> 08:57:58,719
Why?

6454
08:58:01,239 --> 08:58:06,211
Because my grandfather's city was destroyed by men
who could not be stopped and were not

6455
08:58:06,231 --> 08:58:11,033
managed. Nobody tried to manage them. They tried to
appease them, and then they tried

6456
08:58:11,053 --> 08:58:15,969
to fight them, and both were catastrophes, and my
grandfather was nine years old in the

6457
08:58:15,989 --> 08:58:16,707
middle of it.

6458
08:58:18,107 --> 08:58:22,781
I cannot stop you. I have known that for nineteen
years, and I have written it in four

6459
08:58:22,801 --> 08:58:27,584
assessments, each of which was read by fewer people
than the last. So I will manage you.

6460
08:58:27,604 --> 08:58:32,333
For as long as I am alive, and then I will hand the
file to someone else, with the map,

6461
08:58:32,353 --> 08:58:33,916
and they will manage you too.

6462
08:58:35,816 --> 08:58:41,298
That is the entire policy of the People's Republic of
China toward Albert Wesker. I wrote

6463
08:58:41,318 --> 08:58:45,131
it. It is one sentence long, and it is:
keep him at the table.

6464
08:58:48,150 --> 08:58:50,039
He looked at her for a long time.

6465
08:58:50,729 --> 08:58:54,311
That's the best policy anyone on this
planet has about me.

6466
08:58:54,830 --> 08:58:57,992
I know. It is also the only one
that has ever worked.

6467
08:59:00,511 --> 08:59:02,676
One government did not draw a map.

6468
08:59:03,246 --> 08:59:09,114
Colonel Arkady Belov was sixty-nine years old and
had been retired twice, and had both

6469
08:59:09,134 --> 08:59:15,001
times been brought back, because there was no one
else in the Federal Security Service

6470
08:59:15,021 --> 08:59:20,272
who had spent sixteen years on a single file
and could recite it from memory.

6471
08:59:20,842 --> 08:59:26,753
He had never been promoted past colonel. That was
deliberate; colonels can be disowned.

6472
08:59:26,773 --> 08:59:32,615
He had an office with a window, a photograph of
twelve men on his desk, and the quiet,

6473
08:59:32,635 --> 08:59:38,409
complete support of exactly four people in the
Russian state, none of whom would ever

6474
08:59:38,429 --> 08:59:40,044
put anything in writing.

6475
08:59:42,114 --> 08:59:47,399
He had told their mothers about Mali himself, in
their kitchens, in twenty thirty. He

6476
08:59:47,419 --> 08:59:52,705
had been lying, and he had known he was lying, and
three of them had known it too and

6477
08:59:52,725 --> 08:59:53,892
had let him finish.

6478
08:59:54,462 --> 09:00:00,691
In twenty forty-six, the arithmetic finally arrived
at a number he could use. Umbrella's

6479
09:00:00,710 --> 09:00:06,868
Territory sat in the middle of the Atlantic, four
kilometres across, with a hundred and

6480
09:00:06,888 --> 09:00:13,400
sixty thousand people on it and no air defence that
anyone could identify, because a private

6481
09:00:13,419 --> 09:00:16,382
corporation could not legally possess one.

6482
09:00:17,071 --> 09:00:22,107
It is a city on a raft. And he is on it
two hundred days a year.

6483
09:00:24,627 --> 09:00:30,576
The order that went to the submarine was not a Russian
state order. This has been established,

6484
09:00:30,596 --> 09:00:36,354
as far as anything is ever established, by three
separate inquiries. It came from a colonel

6485
09:00:36,374 --> 09:00:42,132
with four friends and a photograph on his desk,
through a chain of people who each believed

6486
09:00:42,152 --> 09:00:46,767
it came from someone above them, and it took
nineteen months to assemble.

6487
09:00:47,337 --> 09:00:53,194
What left the water off the Norwegian coast at four
in the morning on the nineteenth of

6488
09:00:53,214 --> 09:00:59,071
November was a single ballistic missile with a
conventional warhead — a very large one,

6489
09:00:59,091 --> 09:01:05,083
of the kind designed for hardened bunkers — on a
ballistic profile that would put it into

6490
09:01:05,103 --> 09:01:09,339
the Atlantic, on Arklay Free Territory,
eighteen minutes later.

6491
09:01:13,408 --> 09:01:19,504
Eleven governments saw it launch. Four of them had,
by then, standing instructions about

6492
09:01:19,524 --> 09:01:25,759
what to do if anything was ever launched at Arklay,
and all four did the same thing, which

6493
09:01:25,779 --> 09:01:27,566
was to telephone Umbrella.

6494
09:01:28,136 --> 09:01:31,656
They need not have bothered. Umbrella
had seen it first.

6495
09:01:34,476 --> 09:01:37,692
Purchase confirmed. Aegis lattice.

6496
09:01:41,076 --> 09:01:46,674
He had bought it fourteen months before, after the
second attempt on his life, and it

6497
09:01:46,694 --> 09:01:52,556
had sat in orbit doing nothing, in four hundred and
eleven pieces that every space agency

6498
09:01:52,576 --> 09:01:57,117
on Earth had catalogued as a commercial
communications constellation.

6499
09:01:57,687 --> 09:02:00,427
It was not a communications constellation.

6500
09:02:02,496 --> 09:02:08,471
The intercept happened at an altitude of three hundred
and ten kilometres, over the Denmark

6501
09:02:08,491 --> 09:02:11,896
Strait, nine minutes and forty
seconds after launch.

6502
09:02:12,467 --> 09:02:17,993
A hundred and sixty thousand people on Arklay Free
Territory saw a silent white flash,

6503
09:02:18,013 --> 09:02:23,540
very high up and very far to the north, like a star
that came on for a second and then

6504
09:02:23,560 --> 09:02:29,344
went out. Most of them thought it was a meteor. The
ones on the night shift in the harbour

6505
09:02:29,364 --> 09:02:35,342
took photographs of it, which went online within the
hour, and which Tomás Reyes's department

6506
09:02:35,362 --> 09:02:40,244
did not suppress, because there was nothing to
suppress: a light in the sky.

6507
09:02:42,813 --> 09:02:48,825
The Director was awake. He had been awake since the
launch, nine minutes and forty seconds

6508
09:02:48,845 --> 09:02:54,856
of which he had spent in the Thought Acceleration,
which is a subjective ninety-six hours,

6509
09:02:54,876 --> 09:02:58,743
most of which he had spent deciding
what to do afterwards.

6510
09:02:59,313 --> 09:03:01,633
What he decided was: nothing.

6511
09:03:03,823 --> 09:03:04,784
Nothing.

6512
09:03:05,304 --> 09:03:10,910
Nothing public. No statement, no accusation, no
retaliation, no demand. Somebody fired

6513
09:03:10,930 --> 09:03:16,471
a bunker-buster at a civilian city of a hundred and
sixty thousand people and a light

6514
09:03:16,491 --> 09:03:22,621
came on in the sky for one second and went out. That is
the entire story. Let every government

6515
09:03:22,641 --> 09:03:28,183
on Earth work out for themselves what just
happened, and let every one of them arrive

6516
09:03:28,203 --> 09:03:33,875
at the same conclusion in private, and let none of
them ever be able to say it out loud

6517
09:03:33,895 --> 09:03:36,622
without admitting that they were watching.

6518
09:03:37,142 --> 09:03:41,537
You are teaching them a lesson that
has no words in it.

6519
09:03:42,058 --> 09:03:44,034
Those are the only lessons that last.

6520
09:03:46,554 --> 09:03:52,397
Nineteen governments understood, between four and six
o'clock that morning, that Umbrella

6521
09:03:52,417 --> 09:03:58,129
Life Sciences had a functioning global ballistic
missile defence system, which no state

6522
09:03:58,149 --> 09:04:02,016
on Earth possessed, and which it had
chosen not to mention.

6523
09:04:02,587 --> 09:04:08,070
The word for what that made Umbrella is not a
corporate word. Every foreign ministry on

6524
09:04:08,090 --> 09:04:12,941
the planet found the correct word within a
week, and none of them printed it.

6525
09:04:15,510 --> 09:04:21,198
Arkady Belov was not arrested. That would have
required a record of the order.

6526
09:04:21,770 --> 09:04:27,759
He was retired for the third time, in January of
twenty forty-seven, with a pension and

6527
09:04:27,779 --> 09:04:33,699
a medal for long service, and he went to a house
outside Tver that had belonged to his

6528
09:04:33,719 --> 09:04:37,430
wife's family, and he lived there
for four more years.

6529
09:04:38,000 --> 09:04:44,257
He was found, in twenty fifty-one, in the chair by
the window. The photograph of twelve

6530
09:04:44,277 --> 09:04:50,390
men was on the table beside him. The inquiry into
his death, such as it was, recorded

6531
09:04:50,410 --> 09:04:56,668
natural causes, and nobody in any of four
intelligence services believed it, and nobody

6532
09:04:56,688 --> 09:05:01,574
in any of four intelligence services asked
a second question either.

6533
09:05:04,145 --> 09:05:09,581
The Director did not order it. That is worth saying
plainly, because by twenty fifty-one

6534
09:05:09,601 --> 09:05:13,177
it had stopped being the kind of thing
he needed to order.

6535
09:05:13,746 --> 09:05:19,305
Somewhere in an organisation of four hundred and
eighty thousand people, some of whom

6536
09:05:19,325 --> 09:05:24,884
were not people, somebody had worked out what would
be useful. That is what an empire

6537
09:05:24,904 --> 09:05:30,593
is. It is the point at which the will at the top no
longer has to be expressed, because

6538
09:05:30,613 --> 09:05:32,169
it has been distributed.

6539
09:05:35,738 --> 09:05:41,453
He walked back to the guest house. It was three
kilometres, and it was cold, and he had

6540
09:05:41,473 --> 09:05:45,078
no security, and nobody in Beijing
looked at him twice.

6541
09:05:46,769 --> 09:05:47,992
She named us.

6542
09:05:48,511 --> 09:05:49,472
She named you.

6543
09:05:49,992 --> 09:05:57,554
She named the shape of a sentence. It is the same
thing. I built that shape in beer halls

6544
09:05:57,574 --> 09:06:02,410
when the men who built the first
radios were still alive.

6545
09:06:04,309 --> 09:06:05,789
Does it trouble you?

6546
09:06:06,309 --> 09:06:07,964
No. That's what troubles me.

6547
09:06:10,485 --> 09:06:11,877
He walked for a while.

6548
09:06:12,567 --> 09:06:17,280
Twenty years ago it would have. Twenty years ago
I'd have spent the night working out

6549
09:06:17,300 --> 09:06:22,126
how to remove her. And tonight I sat at a table with
a woman who has heard exactly what

6550
09:06:22,146 --> 09:06:26,971
is inside my head, and I drew a map with her, and
I'm walking home in the cold thinking

6551
09:06:26,991 --> 09:06:31,872
that she is the best adversary I will ever have and
that I would like her to live a long

6552
09:06:31,892 --> 09:06:32,150
time.

6553
09:06:32,670 --> 09:06:33,973
You have grown.

6554
09:06:34,493 --> 09:06:38,718
I've grown comfortable. It's not the same
thing, and it's more dangerous.

6555
09:06:41,238 --> 09:06:46,372
He stopped under a lantern and looked at his own
reflection in a closed shop window.

6556
09:06:46,943 --> 09:06:50,131
Ninety-seven percent. Zero divergences.

6557
09:06:50,702 --> 09:06:56,437
He had stopped arguing with the voice in his head, and
he had told himself that this meant

6558
09:06:56,457 --> 09:07:01,872
he had won the argument. Standing in a cold street
in Beijing at midnight, he allowed

6559
09:07:01,892 --> 09:07:06,156
himself, for about four seconds, to
consider the other possibility.

6560
09:07:21,843 --> 09:07:27,933
They called it the Accord, and the negotiation took
four years, and the signing took nineteen

6561
09:07:27,953 --> 09:07:28,458
minutes.

6562
09:07:29,028 --> 09:07:34,852
It was not a surrender, and it was not a conquest,
and every government that signed it

6563
09:07:34,872 --> 09:07:40,695
went home able to explain to its own people why it
had not lost anything. That was the

6564
09:07:40,715 --> 09:07:46,607
whole design. The Director had spent four years
making sure that every single signatory

6565
09:07:46,627 --> 09:07:50,683
could tell a true story about why
signing was good for them.

6566
09:07:51,253 --> 09:07:57,276
The Global Framework Accord on Biosecurity,
Longevity and Infrastructure was signed by

6567
09:07:57,296 --> 09:08:03,248
a hundred and forty-one states. It established a
joint authority — the Accord Council

6568
09:08:03,268 --> 09:08:09,572
— with binding powers over the manufacture and
distribution of a defined list of essential

6569
09:08:09,592 --> 09:08:15,686
medicines, over pandemic response, over biosafety
standards, and over a fund for water,

6570
09:08:15,706 --> 09:08:20,885
power, and health infrastructure in any
signatory state that requested it.

6571
09:08:21,456 --> 09:08:27,586
The Council had thirty-one seats. Fourteen were held
by states, rotating. Nine were held

6572
09:08:27,606 --> 09:08:33,876
by regional blocs. Four were held by the World Health
Organization and other international

6573
09:08:33,896 --> 09:08:39,816
bodies. And four were held by Umbrella Life
Sciences, which also, under Article Nine,

6574
09:08:39,836 --> 09:08:45,966
served as the Council's sole executing agent, because
it was the only body on Earth with

6575
09:08:45,986 --> 09:08:48,272
the capacity to execute anything.

6576
09:08:50,343 --> 09:08:55,959
Four seats out of thirty-one. That was the number in
every newspaper. Every government

6577
09:08:55,979 --> 09:08:57,139
could point at it.

6578
09:08:57,709 --> 09:08:59,981
Article Nine was in the annexes.

6579
09:09:02,551 --> 09:09:07,141
Catherine Adeyemi had drafted Article
Nine. She was fifty-nine.

6580
09:09:07,711 --> 09:09:13,199
She had argued against it for two years, in memos
that were read and answered courteously

6581
09:09:13,219 --> 09:09:18,583
and in full, and then she had drafted it, because
she was the best in the world at that

6582
09:09:18,603 --> 09:09:23,906
kind of drafting and because if she had not done it,
one of the quiet ones would have,

6583
09:09:23,926 --> 09:09:25,700
and it would have been worse.

6584
09:09:26,271 --> 09:09:32,377
She had, by then, developed a private test. Before she
signed anything, she asked herself:

6585
09:09:32,397 --> 09:09:38,368
if I explain this, in plain language, to the woman I
was in twenty twenty-seven, sitting

6586
09:09:38,388 --> 09:09:42,045
in a hedge fund in Manhattan, would
she understand it?

6587
09:09:42,614 --> 09:09:48,753
Article Nine failed the test. She drafted it anyway.
It was the eleventh thing that year

6588
09:09:48,773 --> 09:09:49,942
to fail the test.

6589
09:09:52,512 --> 09:09:57,878
The crowd was not planned. That has been disputed
for two centuries and it is true.

6590
09:09:58,449 --> 09:10:04,141
Tomás Reyes's department had organised a public
broadcast of the signing on screens in

6591
09:10:04,161 --> 09:10:10,053
the Place des Nations, expecting perhaps twenty
thousand people. By four in the afternoon

6592
09:10:10,073 --> 09:10:15,965
there were two hundred thousand in the square and the
streets around it, and by six there

6593
09:10:15,985 --> 09:10:21,744
were four hundred thousand, and the city of Geneva
had closed the bridges and given up.

6594
09:10:22,314 --> 09:10:28,544
They had come from everywhere. A great many of them had
come from the association territories,

6595
09:10:28,564 --> 09:10:34,660
on buses and ferries, at their own expense. There were,
by the estimate of the Swiss police,

6596
09:10:34,680 --> 09:10:38,382
people from a hundred and nine
countries in that square.

6597
09:10:40,452 --> 09:10:45,998
Why they came is the question that matters, and the
answer is the least dramatic thing

6598
09:10:46,018 --> 09:10:47,357
in this entire story.

6599
09:10:47,927 --> 09:10:53,348
Most of them were not fanatics. Most of them had
never said the Creed. They came because

6600
09:10:53,368 --> 09:10:58,664
in twenty forty-seven the world had been frightening
for a very long time, and because

6601
09:10:58,684 --> 09:11:04,043
a single organisation had, in their own direct
experience, vaccinated them, and rebuilt

6602
09:11:04,063 --> 09:11:09,607
their hospital, and put their water back on, and made
their grandmother walk — and because

6603
09:11:09,627 --> 09:11:14,923
something was being signed in their city that felt,
for the first time in their lives,

6604
09:11:14,943 --> 09:11:16,655
like the adults had arrived.

6605
09:11:17,225 --> 09:11:20,492
That is how it happens. Not with
hatred. With relief.

6606
09:11:23,062 --> 09:11:25,381
He came out onto the balcony at seven.

6607
09:11:25,951 --> 09:11:32,025
He had not been scheduled to speak. The programme had
the Secretary-General, and the President

6608
09:11:32,045 --> 09:11:37,666
of the Swiss Confederation, and then the anthem. But
the crowd had begun, at about half

6609
09:11:37,686 --> 09:11:43,241
past six, to make a noise that the people on the
balcony could feel through the stone,

6610
09:11:43,261 --> 09:11:49,011
and the Secretary-General of the United Nations — who
was seventy-four, and who had spent

6611
09:11:49,031 --> 09:11:54,651
his entire career in rooms exactly like the one
behind him — looked out at four hundred

6612
09:11:54,671 --> 09:12:00,550
thousand people and understood that if somebody did
not go out onto that balcony, something

6613
09:12:00,570 --> 09:12:02,755
would happen in Geneva that night.

6614
09:12:03,325 --> 09:12:07,614
So he turned to the man in the black coat and
said: they are calling for you.

6615
09:12:12,183 --> 09:12:15,034
The roar when he stepped out
lasted four minutes.

6616
09:12:15,604 --> 09:12:21,627
He stood at the rail and let it. He did not raise a
hand. He did not smile. He stood perfectly

6617
09:12:21,647 --> 09:12:27,092
still in the floodlights, and four hundred thousand
people shouted themselves hoarse,

6618
09:12:27,112 --> 09:12:33,200
and nineteen thousand kilometres of network carried it
live to an audience that the measurement

6619
09:12:33,220 --> 09:12:38,729
companies afterwards put at six point one billion —
which is to say, everyone on Earth

6620
09:12:38,749 --> 09:12:40,722
who was awake and had a screen.

6621
09:12:43,413 --> 09:12:49,177
Twenty-one years ago I sat in a chair in a building
nobody had ever heard of, in a town

6622
09:12:49,197 --> 09:12:52,502
nobody writes songs about, and I
watched the rain.

6623
09:12:53,902 --> 09:12:56,649
There were six of us. We could not
make the payroll.

6624
09:12:58,669 --> 09:13:03,654
Four hundred thousand people laughed — a
strange, enormous, loving sound.

6625
09:13:04,344 --> 09:13:09,715
Today a hundred and forty-one governments signed a
piece of paper that says something

6626
09:13:09,735 --> 09:13:15,232
very simple. It says that the things which keep
human beings alive are too important to

6627
09:13:15,252 --> 09:13:20,431
be left to chance, or to markets, or to the
electoral calendar of any one country.

6628
09:13:20,832 --> 09:13:25,436
It says that when the storm comes — and it is
coming, and all of you know it, and you

6629
09:13:25,456 --> 09:13:29,409
have known it your whole lives — there will
be something over your heads.

6630
09:13:31,308 --> 09:13:36,546
I did not build that for you. I want to be honest with
you tonight, because you have given

6631
09:13:36,566 --> 09:13:41,394
me something that nobody gives anybody anymore,
and I will not repay it with a lie.

6632
09:13:42,794 --> 09:13:48,075
I did not build it out of love for you. I built it
because the world was badly run, and

6633
09:13:48,095 --> 09:13:51,243
it offended me, and I believed I
could do it better.

6634
09:13:53,144 --> 09:13:58,406
But it is over your heads now. And it does not
matter in the slightest why I built it.

6635
09:14:01,426 --> 09:14:07,461
That was the most dangerous thing anyone said in the
twenty-first century, and six billion

6636
09:14:07,481 --> 09:14:10,354
people heard it, and almost
nobody noticed.

6637
09:14:10,923 --> 09:14:16,819
He had told them the truth. He had told them, from a
balcony, in front of the entire species,

6638
09:14:16,839 --> 09:14:22,289
that he did not love them, that he considered the
world his to correct, and that their

6639
09:14:22,309 --> 09:14:24,707
opinion of his motives was irrelevant.

6640
09:14:25,277 --> 09:14:31,103
And four hundred thousand people in the Place des
Nations heard a man being honest with

6641
09:14:31,123 --> 09:14:36,816
them, which nobody in power had been in their
lifetimes, and they loved him for it so

6642
09:14:36,836 --> 09:14:42,596
completely that the sound they made cracked two
windows on the façade of the Palace of

6643
09:14:42,616 --> 09:14:43,134
Nations.

6644
09:14:45,705 --> 09:14:51,771
The chant began in the south-west corner, among the
buses from the association territories.

6645
09:14:52,341 --> 09:14:53,689
Um. Brel. La.

6646
09:14:54,257 --> 09:15:00,116
It went across four hundred thousand people in about
ninety seconds. It was audible in

6647
09:15:00,136 --> 09:15:06,064
France. Seismographs at the university recorded it.
In the Palace behind him, a hundred

6648
09:15:06,084 --> 09:15:11,327
and forty-one delegations stood at the windows
and watched their century end.

6649
09:15:14,897 --> 09:15:21,088
And on the balcony, in the floodlights, a man who had
died in a bunker in nineteen forty-five

6650
09:15:21,108 --> 09:15:26,832
and a man who had died in a volcano in another world
stood in one body and listened to

6651
09:15:26,852 --> 09:15:32,708
four hundred thousand people chant, and for the first
time in twenty-one years there was

6652
09:15:32,728 --> 09:15:34,846
no argument between them at all.

6653
09:15:35,416 --> 09:15:38,541
No disagreement. No friction.
Not one word.

6654
09:15:40,731 --> 09:15:41,408
Now.

6655
09:15:41,928 --> 09:15:42,868
Now.

6656
09:15:44,387 --> 09:15:49,544
They said it at the same instant, in the same
cadence, in the quiet of one skull.

6657
09:15:50,114 --> 09:15:55,995
And then, for the first time, they said the next
sentence together — one voice, in two

6658
09:15:56,015 --> 09:16:00,045
registers, perfectly aligned, the way
a chord is one sound.

6659
09:16:01,735 --> 09:16:03,336
This is what it was for.

6660
09:16:07,486 --> 09:16:13,013
Integration complete. Host coherence,
one hundred percent.

6661
09:16:16,602 --> 09:16:22,094
He read the panel on the balcony, in the floodlights,
with the chant going on underneath

6662
09:16:22,114 --> 09:16:23,159
him like weather.

6663
09:16:23,728 --> 09:16:29,834
Designation: Wesker. The System had stopped listing a
secondary imprint. It had stopped,

6664
09:16:29,854 --> 09:16:34,499
at some point that it did not specify,
treating them as two things.

6665
09:16:35,068 --> 09:16:41,033
He waited to feel something about that. A loss,
perhaps. The old voice had been in there

6666
09:16:41,053 --> 09:16:47,154
for twenty-one years; it had argued with him in a
thousand cars on a thousand drives home;

6667
09:16:47,174 --> 09:16:52,255
it had been wrong about almost everything and
honest about it exactly once.

6668
09:16:52,824 --> 09:16:56,798
He felt nothing at all. There was nobody
left in there to miss.

6669
09:17:00,367 --> 09:17:06,272
The Umbrella Directorate was established eleven
weeks later, and it was not announced,

6670
09:17:06,292 --> 09:17:12,266
because it was not an announceable thing. It was
simply the name that people inside the

6671
09:17:12,286 --> 09:17:18,190
organisation began to use, in twenty forty-seven,
for the body that made the decisions

6672
09:17:18,210 --> 09:17:24,597
— the Accord Council's executing agent, plus the
Territory, plus the association territories,

6673
09:17:24,617 --> 09:17:30,728
plus the Security Service, plus the Foundation, plus
the Progenitor Initiative, plus four

6674
09:17:30,748 --> 09:17:37,066
hundred and eighty thousand employees and a hundred and
ninety million people in territories

6675
09:17:37,086 --> 09:17:38,100
of association.

6676
09:17:38,669 --> 09:17:44,523
It had one Director. The title had been on his office
door in a four-storey brick building

6677
09:17:44,543 --> 09:17:49,939
in twenty twenty-six, and he had never changed it,
and now it meant something else.

6678
09:17:53,260 --> 09:17:54,669
Level one hundred.

6679
09:17:59,110 --> 09:18:00,181
Status.

6680
09:18:06,760 --> 09:18:12,572
And on the night of the twenty-second of June, twenty
forty-seven, alone in a white room

6681
09:18:12,592 --> 09:18:18,603
two hundred metres below the Atlantic, the Shop that
he had been buying from for twenty-one

6682
09:18:18,623 --> 09:18:19,995
years grew a new tab.

6683
09:18:20,564 --> 09:18:27,165
It had been the same six categories since the first night
in a washroom in the rain. Facilities.

6684
09:18:27,185 --> 09:18:30,751
Personnel. Blueprints. Powers.
Immunities. Vehicles.

6685
09:18:31,321 --> 09:18:37,308
There was a seventh now. It was not lit. It had one
word on it, and when he looked directly

6686
09:18:37,328 --> 09:18:42,986
at it, the word did not resolve into anything he
could read — except that he knew, the

6687
09:18:43,006 --> 09:18:46,419
way you know things in dreams,
exactly what it said.

6688
09:18:49,740 --> 09:18:50,856
Beyond.

6689
09:18:55,444 --> 09:18:57,404
He looked at it for a long time.

6690
09:18:57,975 --> 09:19:03,940
Behind him, in a cradle that had been breathing for
twenty-one years, something enormous

6691
09:19:03,960 --> 09:19:09,993
slept. Above him, two hundred metres of ocean, and a
city of a hundred and sixty thousand

6692
09:19:10,013 --> 09:19:12,782
people, and a world that had just signed.

6693
09:19:13,351 --> 09:19:15,687
He had ruled the Earth for four hours.

6694
09:19:42,055 --> 09:19:45,662
Nobody tells you what it is like the
day after you win.

6695
09:19:46,232 --> 09:19:52,074
The stories all stop at the balcony. The crowd
chants, the banner goes up, the panel says

6696
09:19:52,094 --> 09:19:57,673
integration complete, and the curtain comes down —
because the interesting part, in a

6697
09:19:57,693 --> 09:20:03,469
story, is the getting. Nobody writes the part where
the man who has taken the world sits

6698
09:20:03,489 --> 09:20:08,014
down on a Tuesday morning in front of nine
hundred pages about water.

6699
09:20:08,584 --> 09:20:14,440
That is what the first years of the Umbrella
Directorate actually were. Water. Grain.

6700
09:20:14,460 --> 09:20:20,385
Antibiotics. Power grids in four hundred cities that
had been deferred for forty years

6701
09:20:20,405 --> 09:20:24,947
by governments that would not be in office
when the bill came due.

6702
09:20:27,017 --> 09:20:32,828
He was good at it. That is the part the narrator has
to say plainly, because it is the

6703
09:20:32,848 --> 09:20:35,134
reason none of it was ever undone.

6704
09:20:35,705 --> 09:20:41,479
In the first decade of the Directorate, global
childhood mortality fell by seventy-one

6705
09:20:41,499 --> 09:20:47,409
percent. Four hundred million people were connected
to a reliable electricity supply for

6706
09:20:47,429 --> 09:20:53,271
the first time. The Sahel water programme, which
nineteen international bodies had been

6707
09:20:53,291 --> 09:20:59,066
unable to fund for thirty years, was built in six,
because one entity decided to build

6708
09:20:59,086 --> 09:21:02,435
it and no committee was permitted
to slow it down.

6709
09:21:03,006 --> 09:21:09,013
He did not do it out of compassion. He had said so
from a balcony, in front of six billion

6710
09:21:09,033 --> 09:21:14,772
people, and nobody had listened. He did it because a
badly-run world offended him, and

6711
09:21:14,792 --> 09:21:20,598
because a population that is fed, watered, and
healthy produces more, resists less, and

6712
09:21:20,618 --> 09:21:26,558
— the System was very clear on this point, in panels
he read every morning — pays better.

6713
09:21:29,878 --> 09:21:31,622
Assessment. Quarterly.

6714
09:21:37,603 --> 09:21:39,248
Nought point four percent.

6715
09:21:39,818 --> 09:21:45,827
Thirty-five million people, spread across a planet
of nearly nine billion, who did not

6716
09:21:45,847 --> 09:21:51,785
agree. The System counted them every quarter, in a
line of small text, and never once

6717
09:21:51,805 --> 09:21:54,027
suggested what to do about them.

6718
09:21:56,597 --> 09:22:03,146
Doctor Nadia Okafor was sixty-four years old and had
