7116
09:56:46,148 --> 09:56:51,367
a human being could read, and it spoke English
with the warmth of a good doctor.

7117
09:56:52,058 --> 09:56:56,894
Director. Welcome. You are the two hundred and
eleventh species we have opened an account

7118
09:56:56,914 --> 09:56:59,022
with. May I tell you how this proceeds?

7119
09:56:59,540 --> 09:57:00,181
Please.

7120
09:57:00,703 --> 09:57:04,764
We buy. Your world produces four things of interest
to the Compact, three of which you

7121
09:57:04,784 --> 09:57:09,178
do not presently value. We will pay well. In exchange
we sell: medicine beyond your medicine,

7122
09:57:09,198 --> 09:57:13,259
power beyond your power, and passage. Within forty
of your years you will be a wealthy

7123
09:57:13,279 --> 09:57:17,341
species. Within four hundred you will be a member in
good standing. We ask nothing but

7124
09:57:17,361 --> 09:57:17,911
the account.

7125
09:57:19,930 --> 09:57:20,849
And the terms?

7126
09:57:21,368 --> 09:57:26,501
Standard. Exclusivity of trade. Non-development of
certain technologies, which are listed.

7127
09:57:26,521 --> 09:57:31,824
Non-expansion beyond your system for one hundred years,
after which the boundary is reviewed.

7128
09:57:31,844 --> 09:57:33,255
And the customary surety.

7129
09:57:33,776 --> 09:57:34,525
Which is?

7130
09:57:36,044 --> 09:57:41,942
A registered claim over the system itself. It is a
formality. It has never once been exercised

7131
09:57:41,962 --> 09:57:43,390
in nine thousand years.

7132
09:57:45,910 --> 09:57:47,814
He did not answer for a while.

7133
09:57:48,382 --> 09:57:54,088
He had, by then, spent forty-eight years reading rooms
full of people who wanted something

7134
09:57:54,108 --> 09:57:59,495
from him, and it turned out that the skill
transferred, because the Broker's body had

7135
09:57:59,515 --> 09:58:05,221
a posture and its posture had a grammar, and the
grammar said: this has worked two hundred

7136
09:58:05,241 --> 09:58:06,112
and ten times.

7137
09:58:06,683 --> 09:58:12,947
In the Thought Acceleration — which was, by twenty
seventy-four, running at four thousand

7138
09:58:12,967 --> 09:58:18,879
to one, in nine parallel threads — he took a
subjective afternoon to think about it.

7139
09:58:19,448 --> 09:58:24,808
He thought about a licence agreement with the word
non-exclusive on page three, and a

7140
09:58:24,828 --> 09:58:30,251
landlord who had not read section nine, and a board
of directors who had not read page

7141
09:58:30,271 --> 09:58:35,758
eleven. He thought about how you take a thing from
people who believe they are the ones

7142
09:58:35,778 --> 09:58:41,391
doing the taking, and he recognised, in every line of
the Broker's offer, the exact shape

7143
09:58:41,411 --> 09:58:42,403
of his own work.

7144
09:58:42,973 --> 09:58:46,772
Then he came back, and it had been a fifth
of a second, and he said:

7145
09:58:48,963 --> 09:58:49,583
No.

7146
09:58:52,602 --> 09:58:55,126
I do not think you understand the offer.

7147
09:58:55,646 --> 09:59:01,235
I understand it perfectly. You've made it two hundred
and ten times. Let me tell you what

7148
09:59:01,255 --> 09:59:01,613
it is.

7149
09:59:03,014 --> 09:59:07,882
You will pay us handsomely for four things, three of
which we do not know the value of,

7150
09:59:07,902 --> 09:59:12,771
which means you will pay us a fraction of what they
are worth and we will be delighted,

7151
09:59:12,791 --> 09:59:17,547
because we have nothing to compare it to. You will
sell us medicine and power, and in

7152
09:59:17,567 --> 09:59:22,492
forty years we will be unable to manufacture either
for ourselves, because why would we,

7153
09:59:22,512 --> 09:59:27,325
when you sell it so cheaply. The non-development
list is not a safety measure; it is a

7154
09:59:27,345 --> 09:59:32,270
list of every technology by which a client stops
being a client. And the surety over our

7155
09:59:32,290 --> 09:59:37,046
system is a formality that has never been exercised
because it has never needed to be

7156
09:59:37,066 --> 09:59:41,935
— because by the time exercising it would be worth
your while, no species has ever been

7157
09:59:41,955 --> 09:59:43,340
in a condition to object.

7158
09:59:45,240 --> 09:59:50,806
You are not offering us an account. You are offering
us dependency, on a schedule, with

7159
09:59:50,826 --> 09:59:52,925
a lien on our home as collateral.

7160
09:59:55,445 --> 10:00:01,625
The chamber did something. It was not a sound. The
light in it changed, slightly, in a

7161
10:00:01,645 --> 10:00:05,879
way that eleven species understood and
four humans did not.

7162
10:00:06,568 --> 10:00:09,545
That is an unusually complete reading.

7163
10:00:10,065 --> 10:00:16,256
I've made the same offer myself. Forty years ago, to a
landlord in Delaware, for a building.

7164
10:00:16,276 --> 10:00:17,741
It worked beautifully.

7165
10:00:20,261 --> 10:00:25,508
Then you will understand that refusal has a cost. The
Compact does not make war on markets.

7166
10:00:25,528 --> 10:00:30,659
But a world that declines the account is not a
market. It is a curiosity. And curiosities

7167
10:00:30,679 --> 10:00:31,933
are visited by others.

7168
10:00:32,452 --> 10:00:33,029
Who?

7169
10:00:33,549 --> 10:00:37,445
The Veth Hegemony is nine hundred light years from
your star and has been informed of

7170
10:00:37,465 --> 10:00:41,407
your existence since your first radio. They do not
buy. They do not sell. They arrive,

7171
10:00:41,427 --> 10:00:45,369
and they assess, and what they find useful they
administer, and what they find useless

7172
10:00:45,389 --> 10:00:49,377
they clear. We are, Director, the only wall between
your species and that. That is what

7173
10:00:49,397 --> 10:00:53,338
you are actually being offered, and that is why two
hundred and ten species have taken

7174
10:00:53,358 --> 10:00:53,477
it.

7175
10:00:55,996 --> 10:01:02,429
And that — the Directorate's analysts would conclude,
over the following nine years, reading

7176
10:01:02,449 --> 10:01:08,461
the transcript four thousand times — was the only
genuinely honest sentence the Broker

7177
10:01:08,481 --> 10:01:09,443
spoke all day.

7178
10:01:11,514 --> 10:01:16,983
He took off his sunglasses. He had thought about it
in the shuttle, and had decided it

7179
10:01:17,003 --> 10:01:22,473
was probably meaningless to a species with no faces,
and did it anyway, because it was

7180
10:01:22,493 --> 10:01:23,686
not for the Broker.

7181
10:01:24,376 --> 10:01:28,918
Then let me make a counter-offer, and let me be
as honest as you have just been.

7182
10:01:29,318 --> 10:01:33,539
We will not take your account. We will buy from you,
at market, in cash, and we will sell

7183
10:01:33,559 --> 10:01:37,590
to you, at market, and we will reverse-engineer
every single thing you sell us, which

7184
10:01:37,610 --> 10:01:41,687
you know we will do, and which your non-development
list exists to prevent. We will do

7185
10:01:41,707 --> 10:01:45,785
it anyway. We will be the two hundred and eleventh
species to say no, and probably the

7186
10:01:45,805 --> 10:01:47,930
first, and you will find it
very interesting.

7187
10:01:49,329 --> 10:01:51,613
And when the Veth come, we will
deal with the Veth.

7188
10:01:54,134 --> 10:01:55,910
You have four ships.

7189
10:01:56,429 --> 10:01:58,286
I have had four of something before.

7190
10:02:01,307 --> 10:02:07,279
The nine vessels left the solar system in January of
twenty seventy-five. They did not

7191
10:02:07,299 --> 10:02:13,620
threaten. They did not retaliate. The Compact had not
made war on a market in nine thousand

7192
10:02:13,640 --> 10:02:19,822
years, and a species that had declined the account
was not a market, and they had a great

7193
10:02:19,842 --> 10:02:20,937
deal else to do.

7194
10:02:21,506 --> 10:02:27,837
Before they went, the Broker sent one final private
transmission, addressed to the Director

7195
10:02:27,857 --> 10:02:33,838
personally, in a language that the Farside Array
took four years to confirm was one of

7196
10:02:33,858 --> 10:02:39,909
the Compact's internal trade dialects and not, as
had initially been assumed, an error.

7197
10:02:40,478 --> 10:02:46,837
It was eleven words long. The Directorate has never
published it. It is, however, carved

7198
10:02:46,857 --> 10:02:53,650
— in the original characters, untranslated — above the
door of a room on Arklay Free Territory

7199
10:02:53,670 --> 10:02:56,186
that the public is not admitted to.

7200
10:02:58,376 --> 10:03:02,009
We have met your kind before. We did
not like them either.

7201
10:03:05,529 --> 10:03:09,125
He stood on the bridge of the
Wilmington and watched them go.

7202
10:03:09,693 --> 10:03:15,877
For forty-eight years he had been the most dangerous
thing in every room he had ever entered.

7203
10:03:15,897 --> 10:03:21,613
He had woken in a chair in the rain with a virus in
his blood and a machine in the air

7204
10:03:21,633 --> 10:03:27,550
and had never, in half a century, met anything that
could not be out-thought, out-waited,

7205
10:03:27,570 --> 10:03:28,483
or out-bought.

7206
10:03:29,054 --> 10:03:34,608
And a four-metre creature with no face had just
told him, courteously, that there was

7207
10:03:34,628 --> 10:03:40,183
something nine hundred light years away that
arrived, and assessed, and cleared — and

7208
10:03:40,203 --> 10:03:45,955
that the only reason it had not arrived already was
that a trading company had found his

7209
10:03:45,975 --> 10:03:49,759
species more profitable as a customer
than as a clearance.

7210
10:03:51,829 --> 10:03:55,481
He found, standing on the bridge,
that he was not afraid.

7211
10:03:56,050 --> 10:04:01,861
He examined that carefully, because it was strange,
and because forty-eight years of being

7212
10:04:01,881 --> 10:04:07,692
right had taught him to be suspicious of his own calm.
He was not afraid. He was something

7213
10:04:07,712 --> 10:04:13,200
else, and it took him a subjective hour in the
Thought Acceleration to find the word,

7214
10:04:13,220 --> 10:04:15,792
and when he found it he did not like it.

7215
10:04:17,862 --> 10:04:19,119
He was relieved.

7216
10:04:19,689 --> 10:04:25,180
For twenty-seven years he had owned a species. There
had been nothing left to take. He

7217
10:04:25,200 --> 10:04:30,692
had built the thing he had spent two lifetimes
wanting, and it had been finished for a

7218
10:04:30,712 --> 10:04:36,139
decade, and the ruling of it was administration —
councils, and quotas, and a hundred

7219
10:04:36,159 --> 10:04:39,024
and forty-one governments that
never said no.

7220
10:04:39,593 --> 10:04:44,926
And somewhere nine hundred light years away there
was an empire that had never heard of

7221
10:04:44,946 --> 10:04:45,172
him.

7222
10:04:47,862 --> 10:04:48,759
There you are.

7223
10:04:50,779 --> 10:04:56,352
There was nobody in his head to answer. He had
stopped noticing that a long time ago.

7224
10:04:56,921 --> 10:05:02,391
But if the old voice had still been there — if the
thing that had argued with him in a

7225
10:05:02,411 --> 10:05:08,073
thousand cars, and wept on a balcony, and admitted
once, on a terrace above the Atlantic,

7226
10:05:08,093 --> 10:05:13,563
that it had been wrong about everything except the
goal — if it had been there to hear

7227
10:05:13,583 --> 10:05:17,265
him say it, it would have recognised
the tone immediately.

7228
10:05:37,280 --> 10:05:43,770
The Tollhouse Compact sold humanity four things in
the first year, at market, in cash,

7229
10:05:43,790 --> 10:05:45,132
exactly as agreed.

7230
10:05:45,703 --> 10:05:52,238
A material. A power storage medium. A navigational
reference. And a medical scanner, which

7231
10:05:52,258 --> 10:05:58,502
the Broker's trade division had listed as a courtesy
item and which rendered obsolete,

7232
10:05:58,522 --> 10:06:03,965
in an afternoon, every diagnostic instrument
the human race had ever built.

7233
10:06:04,535 --> 10:06:10,202
The Directorate bought nine of each. It paid in the
four things the Compact wanted from

7234
10:06:10,222 --> 10:06:16,085
Earth, three of which humanity had not known were
valuable, and one of which was a species

7235
10:06:16,105 --> 10:06:21,772
of deep-sea sponge from a trench off the Marianas
that turned out, for reasons no human

7236
10:06:21,792 --> 10:06:26,935
has ever fully understood, to be worth roughly
its weight in finished starship.

7237
10:06:29,005 --> 10:06:32,232
And then Umbrella took all
thirty-six of them apart.

7238
10:06:32,801 --> 10:06:38,841
It took nineteen years. That is the part the popular
histories leave out, because nineteen

7239
10:06:38,861 --> 10:06:44,834
years of failure does not film well. The Compact's
non-development list existed precisely

7240
10:06:44,854 --> 10:06:50,625
because two hundred and ten prior species had tried
exactly this, and the list was not

7241
10:06:50,645 --> 10:06:56,482
a prohibition; it was a prediction, and it had been
accurate two hundred and ten times.

7242
10:06:57,053 --> 10:07:03,437
The power storage medium defeated four generations of
Umbrella's physicists. Sixty years

7243
10:07:03,457 --> 10:07:09,840
later, it still defeats them; the Directorate
manufactures it, in quantity, by a process

7244
10:07:09,860 --> 10:07:14,642
that works reliably and that nobody has
ever been able to explain.

7245
10:07:16,712 --> 10:07:19,825
Sebastian Crane ran it. He was ninety-two.

7246
10:07:20,393 --> 10:07:26,160
He had come to Umbrella in twenty thirty-four,
ruined, dripping on a carpet in a corner

7247
10:07:26,180 --> 10:07:32,214
office, having spent nine billion dollars trying to
build a machine that could model Albert

7248
10:07:32,234 --> 10:07:37,934
Wesker. He had spent the forty-one years since in
windowless rooms, and had never once

7249
10:07:37,954 --> 10:07:41,725
asked for a title, and had never once
left the Territory.

7250
10:07:42,297 --> 10:07:48,268
He was, by twenty seventy-five, the most
accomplished scientist alive, and he was still

7251
10:07:48,288 --> 10:07:54,190
— he said so cheerfully, to anyone who asked —
trying to model the Director, and still

7252
10:07:54,210 --> 10:07:59,287
failing, and had come to regard the failing as
the great work of his life.

7253
10:07:59,977 --> 10:08:05,053
Thirty-six alien devices, Director. We've cracked four.
That's a hit rate of eleven percent.

7254
10:08:05,573 --> 10:08:11,046
Against a species that has been doing this for nine
thousand years and has never lost

7255
10:08:11,066 --> 10:08:11,627
a client.

7256
10:08:12,148 --> 10:08:16,732
That's the first time you've ever put it that way.
Eleven percent is extraordinary.

7257
10:08:17,252 --> 10:08:20,389
Eleven percent is a beginning. How
long for the rest?

7258
10:08:20,910 --> 10:08:25,315
For the scanner and the material, twenty years. For
the storage medium — Albert, honestly?

7259
10:08:25,335 --> 10:08:29,839
I think we may have to grow a generation of physicists
who've never learned why it shouldn't

7260
10:08:29,859 --> 10:08:30,085
work.

7261
10:08:31,603 --> 10:08:32,543
Then grow them.

7262
10:08:35,063 --> 10:08:40,897
They did. There is an institute on Mars, founded in
twenty seventy-nine, whose entire

7263
10:08:40,917 --> 10:08:46,750
curriculum was designed around a deliberate
omission: its students are not taught the

7264
10:08:46,770 --> 10:08:52,810
theory that says the storage medium is impossible
until their fourth year, by which time

7265
10:08:52,830 --> 10:08:55,289
most of them have already built one.

7266
10:08:55,859 --> 10:09:02,255
It is the single most effective educational
programme in human history. It is also, the

7267
10:09:02,275 --> 10:09:08,448
narrator notes, a very precise description of what
the Directorate did to a species.

7268
10:09:11,519 --> 10:09:13,472
He built ships for fifteen years.

7269
10:09:14,043 --> 10:09:20,088
The Wilmington had been one, in twenty sixty-six,
and had cost four trillion Points. By

7270
10:09:20,108 --> 10:09:26,014
twenty seventy-six the pattern had been analysed,
adapted, and — in the four specific

7271
10:09:26,034 --> 10:09:31,940
subsystems that human engineering could improve —
improved, and the Directorate could

7272
10:09:31,960 --> 10:09:35,705
build one in a yard, out of asteroid
metal, for money.

7273
10:09:36,274 --> 10:09:42,437
Nine in twenty seventy-eight. Twenty-nine by
eighty-two. Ninety-one by twenty ninety.

7274
10:09:43,007 --> 10:09:49,624
It was the largest sustained industrial effort in the
history of the species, and it consumed,

7275
10:09:49,644 --> 10:09:55,838
at its peak, four percent of everything the human
race produced, and not one human being

7276
10:09:55,858 --> 10:09:57,674
anywhere ever voted on it.

7277
10:09:59,743 --> 10:10:05,893
Nobody objected. That is not a figure of speech. In
fifteen years, across four hundred

7278
10:10:05,913 --> 10:10:12,565
and eleven billion hours of public communication
monitored by the Directorate's own analysts,

7279
10:10:12,585 --> 10:10:18,878
the total recorded objection to the naval programme
amounted to a fraction of a percent,

7280
10:10:18,898 --> 10:10:22,752
and most of it concerned the choice
of yard locations.

7281
10:10:23,322 --> 10:10:29,465
The reason was that the Broker had been honest, once,
in a chamber that smelled of cinnamon

7282
10:10:29,485 --> 10:10:35,357
and ozone, and the Directorate had published that
sentence in full, on every frequency,

7283
10:10:35,377 --> 10:10:39,692
on every world, within nine hours of the
delegation's departure.

7284
10:10:40,262 --> 10:10:45,773
They arrive, and they assess, and what they find
useful they administer, and what they

7285
10:10:45,793 --> 10:10:47,317
find useless they clear.

7286
10:10:47,887 --> 10:10:53,753
Nine billion people read it. They did not need to be
told anything else for fifteen years.

7287
10:10:56,324 --> 10:10:57,426
An enemy.

7288
10:10:57,995 --> 10:11:03,688
The thought arrived unbidden, in his own voice, in
the room with no name on the door,

7289
10:11:03,708 --> 10:11:09,603
and he examined it carefully, the way he had learned
to examine everything that came out

7290
10:11:09,623 --> 10:11:10,476
of that room.

7291
10:11:11,048 --> 10:11:16,770
The old voice had been wrong about almost everything.
It had been wrong about speed, and

7292
10:11:16,790 --> 10:11:22,448
about banners, and about terror, and about what a
people will hold together around. And

7293
10:11:22,468 --> 10:11:27,995
it had said, on a terrace above the Atlantic in
twenty forty-one: I gave them someone

7294
10:11:28,015 --> 10:11:31,453
to hate, because hate is quick, and
I was in a hurry.

7295
10:11:32,022 --> 10:11:35,598
He had told it, then, that he had given
them a roof instead.

7296
10:11:36,168 --> 10:11:41,984
He stood in a shipyard in twenty eighty-four, watching
the forty-first hull come together,

7297
10:11:42,004 --> 10:11:47,562
and understood that he had just been given something
he had not had to build. An enemy

7298
10:11:47,582 --> 10:11:51,517
that was real, that was coming, and
that he had not invented.

7299
10:11:52,088 --> 10:11:57,938
It was, he thought — and this is recorded, because
he said it aloud to an engineer who

7300
10:11:57,958 --> 10:12:02,649
has left an account — the single greatest
strategic gift of his life.

7301
10:12:05,718 --> 10:12:07,862
The other preparation was Evelyn's.

7302
10:12:08,432 --> 10:12:14,833
The Progenitor Initiative had been a programme of eleven
hundred people in twenty fifty-eight.

7303
10:12:14,853 --> 10:12:20,709
By twenty eighty-eight it was the largest research
organisation that has ever existed,

7304
10:12:20,729 --> 10:12:25,627
and it had a single stated objective, and the
objective was not medical.

7305
10:12:26,197 --> 10:12:32,136
The Directorate needed crews. Nine hundred
void-cutters would need four hundred thousand

7306
10:12:32,156 --> 10:12:38,027
personnel who could tolerate the pattern's
acceleration, its radiation environment, and

7307
10:12:38,047 --> 10:12:44,122
the psychological load of sitting in the dark for four
days without speaking. Human beings

7308
10:12:44,142 --> 10:12:46,018
could do two of those three.

7309
10:12:46,588 --> 10:12:51,928
She solved it in nine years, and the solution is
the reason the Veth called the ships

7310
10:12:51,948 --> 10:12:52,307
wrong.

7311
10:12:52,875 --> 10:12:58,815
The Directorate's crews were not conscripts and not
slaves. Four hundred thousand human

7312
10:12:58,835 --> 10:13:04,774
beings volunteered — genuinely volunteered, with
informed consent documents that ran to

7313
10:13:04,794 --> 10:13:10,733
two hundred pages and were the most honest documents
the Directorate ever produced — to

7314
10:13:10,753 --> 10:13:16,556
receive a derivative of the Progenitor lineage that
would let them survive the ships.

7315
10:13:17,125 --> 10:13:23,110
They knew what it would do. It was in section four of
the consent form, in plain language:

7316
10:13:23,130 --> 10:13:28,914
this will change your relationship to command. You
will find it difficult to experience

7317
10:13:28,934 --> 10:13:35,185
doubt regarding an order from the Directorate. This
effect is permanent and is not reversible.

7318
10:13:35,755 --> 10:13:40,322
Four hundred thousand people signed it. There
were nine million applicants.

7319
10:13:42,892 --> 10:13:49,119
They were not summoned personnel. That distinction
mattered enormously to the Directorate's

7320
10:13:49,139 --> 10:13:55,297
lawyers and mattered not at all to anyone who met
them. They had families, and childhoods,

7321
10:13:55,317 --> 10:13:59,758
and opinions about music. They laughed at
jokes. They wrote home.

7322
10:14:00,329 --> 10:14:05,527
And they sat in the dark for four days at the
heliopause without speaking, and when a

7323
10:14:05,547 --> 10:14:11,053
fleet four hundred vessels strong crossed into their
system, not one of them felt anything

7324
10:14:11,073 --> 10:14:16,334
that a Veth sensor could read as fear, because fear
about an order had been engineered

7325
10:14:16,354 --> 10:14:20,447
out of them in a white room by a woman who
had done the arithmetic.

7326
10:14:23,638 --> 10:14:24,828
Nine million applied.

7327
10:14:25,346 --> 10:14:28,907
For four hundred thousand places. We could
have had forty million.

7328
10:14:29,427 --> 10:14:30,900
Why do you think they did it?

7329
10:14:32,921 --> 10:14:37,910
Because you published the Broker's sentence and
then you built the ships and then you

7330
10:14:37,930 --> 10:14:43,155
asked. In that order. It's the same thing you did in
the break room in twenty twenty-six,

7331
10:14:43,175 --> 10:14:45,808
Albert. It's the only thing
you've ever done.

7332
10:14:47,206 --> 10:14:51,946
You tell people the truth about the storm, and then
you stand where the rain isn't, and

7333
10:14:51,966 --> 10:14:52,712
then you wait.

7334
10:14:55,732 --> 10:15:01,185
In the last year before the Hegemony arrived, he
did something that the Directorate's

7335
10:15:01,205 --> 10:15:04,468
own historians have never
satisfactorily explained.

7336
10:15:05,038 --> 10:15:11,235
He had a wall built. On the outer terrace of the
first ring of Arklay Free Territory,

7337
10:15:11,255 --> 10:15:18,037
facing east, four hundred metres long, of white stone
from the seamount the city was anchored

7338
10:15:18,057 --> 10:15:18,256
to.

7339
10:15:18,826 --> 10:15:21,920
It was empty. It had no names
on it at all.

7340
10:15:22,490 --> 10:15:28,026
The commission specified that it was to be
maintained in perpetuity, that no name was

7341
10:15:28,046 --> 10:15:33,714
ever to be added except that of a person who had
died in the service of the Directorate

7342
10:15:33,734 --> 10:15:39,401
beyond the orbit of the Moon, and that the names
were to be added in the order of their

7343
10:15:39,421 --> 10:15:45,088
dying, with no rank, and no decoration, and no
distinction of any kind between summoned

7344
10:15:45,108 --> 10:15:46,854
personnel and human beings.

7345
10:15:48,923 --> 10:15:55,004
That last clause caused the only serious
institutional argument of his entire reign. Four

7346
10:15:55,024 --> 10:16:01,309
separate bodies of the Directorate objected, on the
entirely reasonable ground that summoned

7347
10:16:01,329 --> 10:16:07,272
personnel were assets, that they had been purchased,
that they did not die in any sense

7348
10:16:07,292 --> 10:16:13,578
that a memorial recognises, and that a wall which
failed to distinguish them from volunteers

7349
10:16:13,598 --> 10:16:15,634
would diminish the volunteers.

7350
10:16:16,205 --> 10:16:22,243
He heard all four objections in full, over nine
hours, and then overruled every one of

7351
10:16:22,263 --> 10:16:27,738
them in a single sentence that is carved, now,
at the eastern end of the wall.

7352
10:16:29,928 --> 10:16:31,331
They stood where I put them.

7353
10:16:34,351 --> 10:16:40,872
Within four years the wall had four thousand names on
it. Within twenty, it had been extended

7354
10:16:40,892 --> 10:16:41,294
twice.

7355
10:16:41,865 --> 10:16:47,229
The narrator has thought about that wall a great
deal, and is not going to tell you what

7356
10:16:47,249 --> 10:16:49,983
it means, because the narrator
does not know.

7357
10:16:50,553 --> 10:16:56,390
Somewhere in a mind that ran nine threads at four
thousand to one, a man who had spent

7358
10:16:56,410 --> 10:17:02,316
a century and a half arranging the truth had ordered
four hundred metres of white stone

7359
10:17:20,953 --> 10:17:26,790
The Veth Hegemony arrived in the spring of twenty
ninety-one, and it did not send a message

7360
10:17:26,810 --> 10:17:27,176
first.

7361
10:17:27,747 --> 10:17:33,935
It had been informed of humanity's existence in
nineteen thirty-six, by a radio broadcast

7362
10:17:33,955 --> 10:17:40,352
of the Berlin Olympic Games, which had crossed nine
hundred light years and been catalogued,

7363
10:17:40,372 --> 10:17:46,211
in the Hegemony's registry of emergent systems, as
a low-priority assessment target.

7364
10:17:46,781 --> 10:17:52,414
The Adolf half of the mind would have found that
exquisitely funny. There was no Adolf

7365
10:17:52,434 --> 10:17:58,132
half of the mind anymore. There was a man who noted
the fact, and filed it in a room on

7366
10:17:58,152 --> 10:18:02,537
the fourth floor of an imaginary brick
building, and did not laugh.

7367
10:18:04,608 --> 10:18:10,537
They came with four hundred and eleven vessels, which
was a routine allocation for a system

7368
10:18:10,557 --> 10:18:16,422
of humanity's assessed development, and which
represented approximately one two-thousandth

7369
10:18:16,442 --> 10:18:18,580
of the Hegemony's standing force.

7370
10:18:19,149 --> 10:18:25,218
The Veth were not cruel. That is the thing every human
account gets wrong, and it is important.

7371
10:18:25,238 --> 10:18:30,986
They were an empire of nine thousand years and four
hundred worlds, organised into a caste

7372
10:18:31,006 --> 10:18:36,562
structure of such antiquity that no living Veth
could remember its origin, and they had

7373
10:18:36,582 --> 10:18:42,074
a doctrine for emergent species that was entirely
rational and had worked four hundred

7374
10:18:42,094 --> 10:18:47,521
times. They arrived. They assessed. What was
useful, they administered. What was not,

7375
10:18:47,541 --> 10:18:48,354
they cleared.

7376
10:18:48,926 --> 10:18:54,569
They did not hate anyone. They had not hated
anything in nine thousand years. That was

7377
10:18:54,589 --> 10:18:56,545
what made them what they were.

7378
10:18:59,113 --> 10:19:05,472
The Veth admiral's name and caste-title together ran
to forty-one syllables. Human records

7379
10:19:05,492 --> 10:19:08,731
call her Sethra-Vel, which was
the first four.

7380
10:19:09,301 --> 10:19:15,199
She had administered nine emergent systems. She had
cleared two. She had held her command

7381
10:19:15,219 --> 10:19:20,916
for four hundred and six years, which was possible
because the Hegemony's upper castes

7382
10:19:20,936 --> 10:19:26,967
lived that long, and which was why the Hegemony's
doctrine had not changed in nine thousand

7383
10:19:26,987 --> 10:19:27,365
years.

7384
10:19:27,936 --> 10:19:33,467
She took her fleet to the edge of the human system on
the fourth of April, and she opened

7385
10:19:33,487 --> 10:19:38,769
her registry, and she read the assessment that had
been compiled from a century and a

7386
10:19:38,789 --> 10:19:40,390
half of intercepted radio.

7387
10:19:40,960 --> 10:19:47,275
What she read was a species that had achieved powered
flight, nuclear fission, and orbital

7388
10:19:47,295 --> 10:19:53,259
capability within a single lifetime; that had
fought two global wars of extraordinary

7389
10:19:53,279 --> 10:19:59,242
savagery; that had fragmented into a hundred and
ninety-three competing polities; and

7390
10:19:59,262 --> 10:20:05,226
that had, in the last four decades, gone
unaccountably quiet in a manner the registry

7391
10:20:05,246 --> 10:20:07,690
flagged as consolidation, probable.

7392
10:20:08,259 --> 10:20:13,852
She ordered a standard approach. Four hundred
vessels, in formation, into the system,

7393
10:20:13,872 --> 10:20:15,898
to the third planet, to assess.

7394
10:20:18,468 --> 10:20:24,618
There were ninety-one void-cutters by twenty
ninety-one. They were waiting at the heliopause,

7395
10:20:24,638 --> 10:20:27,538
in a plane, at rest, with their
drives cold.

7396
10:20:28,108 --> 10:20:32,716
The first thing that went wrong for the Hegemony
was that they could not see them.

7397
10:20:33,287 --> 10:20:38,865
It is not that the void-cutters were invisible. The
Veth had sensors that could count

7398
10:20:38,885 --> 10:20:44,462
the moons of a gas giant from four light years. It
is that the ships did not radiate.

7399
10:20:44,482 --> 10:20:50,256
They did not run beacons, or transponders, or
navigation lights, or communications. They

7400
10:20:50,276 --> 10:20:56,183
did not talk to each other; they had been positioned,
days before, and given their orders,

7401
10:20:56,203 --> 10:20:59,739
and they sat in the dark with
everything off, waiting.

7402
10:21:00,309 --> 10:21:06,271
No navy in nine thousand years had done that, because
no navy in nine thousand years had

7403
10:21:06,291 --> 10:21:12,185
been crewed by people who could be relied upon to
sit in the dark for four days without

7404
10:21:12,205 --> 10:21:13,408
asking a question.

7405
10:21:13,978 --> 10:21:19,858
The Wilmington's bridge crew was ninety-one people.
Eighty-one of them had come from the

7406
10:21:19,878 --> 10:21:25,556
Shop. They sat at their stations for four days in
the dark and did not speak, did not

7407
10:21:25,576 --> 10:21:29,242
fidget, did not eat, and did not
once look at the door.

7408
10:21:29,812 --> 10:21:35,480
The ten who were human found it, they all said
afterwards, the worst four days of their

7409
10:21:35,500 --> 10:21:35,872
lives.

7410
10:21:38,442 --> 10:21:43,639
The second thing that went wrong for the Hegemony was
that the Directorate did not attack

7411
10:21:43,659 --> 10:21:44,226
the fleet.

7412
10:21:44,795 --> 10:21:50,752
Sethra-Vel's formation crossed the heliopause on the
ninth of April and proceeded inward

7413
10:21:50,772 --> 10:21:57,137
for four days, and nothing happened. On the fourth day
her sensor officers reported ninety-one

7414
10:21:57,157 --> 10:22:02,910
objects that had appeared behind her — objects that
had been there all along, and had

7415
10:22:02,930 --> 10:22:08,956
simply begun to exist by lighting their drives, in
formation, across her line of retreat.

7416
10:22:09,526 --> 10:22:16,092
She did what four hundred years of doctrine told her
to do, which was to hold her formation

7417
10:22:16,112 --> 10:22:22,317
and open communications, because an emergent species
that reveals a fleet is a species

7418
10:22:22,337 --> 10:22:24,055
that wants to negotiate.

7419
10:22:24,625 --> 10:22:30,540
The Directorate did not answer. The ninety-one ships
held station behind her, in perfect

7420
10:22:30,560 --> 10:22:33,980
silence, and matched her velocity,
and did nothing.

7421
10:22:36,050 --> 10:22:40,103
She held course for four more days. The
ninety-one followed.

7422
10:22:40,673 --> 10:22:46,668
Her officers requested permission to engage. She
refused, four times, because doctrine

7423
10:22:46,688 --> 10:22:52,963
was clear and because in four hundred and six years
she had never once been in a situation

7424
10:22:52,983 --> 10:22:57,089
in which the other party had failed to
say anything at all.

7425
10:22:57,659 --> 10:23:03,736
On the eighth day, at a range of nine million
kilometres from the third planet, she ordered

7426
10:23:03,756 --> 10:23:05,947
her fleet to decelerate and hold.

7427
10:23:06,517 --> 10:23:11,221
And the moment her formation went to rest,
the ninety-one opened fire.

7428
10:23:13,791 --> 10:23:16,108
The engagement lasted nine minutes.

7429
10:23:16,678 --> 10:23:22,120
The narrator is not going to describe the weapons.
They were bought from a tab in a shop

7430
10:23:22,140 --> 10:23:27,582
that only one man could see, and their operating
principles are not something this story

7431
10:23:27,602 --> 10:23:33,169
is going to explain, and by the twenty-second century
their effects were well enough known

7432
10:23:33,189 --> 10:23:34,535
that there is no need.

7433
10:23:35,105 --> 10:23:41,291
A hundred and eleven Veth vessels were destroyed in
the first ninety seconds. Sethra-Vel's

7434
10:23:41,311 --> 10:23:47,290
fleet returned fire with everything it had, and the
ninety-one void-cutters took damage

7435
10:23:47,310 --> 10:23:53,427
— real damage; four of them were lost with all hands,
and two of the four had human crews

7436
10:23:53,447 --> 10:23:56,738
aboard, and their names are on a
wall on Arklay.

7437
10:23:57,308 --> 10:24:03,167
And then the Veth formation broke, which in nine
thousand years it had done four times,

7438
10:24:03,187 --> 10:24:05,464
and the ninety-one did not pursue.

7439
10:24:08,034 --> 10:24:11,584
Here is the part that mattered, and
it is not the battle.

7440
10:24:12,154 --> 10:24:18,379
Sethra-Vel withdrew to the outer system with two
hundred and ninety-one vessels and waited

7441
10:24:18,399 --> 10:24:24,416
to be pursued, and was not. She waited nine days.
Then she transmitted a formal request

7442
10:24:24,436 --> 10:24:29,899
for terms, which is a thing the Hegemony had
done twice in nine thousand years.

7443
10:24:30,468 --> 10:24:36,202
The Directorate's answer came in forty seconds, in
fluent High Veth, in a grammatical

7444
10:24:36,222 --> 10:24:39,655
register that her caste used for
addressing equals.

7445
10:24:40,344 --> 10:24:45,426
You may withdraw. Your wounded may withdraw with you.
You will leave your registry beacon

7446
10:24:45,446 --> 10:24:49,036
in this system so that the next fleet
knows what happened here.

7447
10:24:50,437 --> 10:24:55,898
Report the following to your Hegemony. This system
is administered. It is not available

7448
10:24:55,918 --> 10:25:01,695
for assessment. We have no interest in your four
hundred worlds and no intention of visiting

7449
10:25:01,715 --> 10:25:05,224
them. If you come again, we will not
stop at your fleet.

7450
10:25:07,743 --> 10:25:09,447
She read it four times.

7451
10:25:10,017 --> 10:25:15,658
In four hundred and six years she had never
received a communication from an emergent

7452
10:25:15,678 --> 10:25:21,785
species that did not contain either a plea or a threat.
This contained neither. It contained

7453
10:25:21,805 --> 10:25:27,712
a boundary, and a consequence, and the courtesy of
her own caste-register, and a sentence

7454
10:25:27,732 --> 10:25:33,572
— we have no interest in your four hundred worlds —
that she understood, immediately and

7455
10:25:33,592 --> 10:25:35,171
completely, to be a lie.

7456
10:25:37,242 --> 10:25:43,273
She wrote in her report — and the Hegemony's
registry is one of the few alien documents

7457
10:25:43,293 --> 10:25:49,254
that human historians have in full, because a beacon
was left in the system exactly as

7458
10:25:49,274 --> 10:25:53,428
instructed — the four sentences for
which she is remembered:

7459
10:25:55,116 --> 10:26:00,644
They do not broadcast. They do not boast. They sat in
the dark for four days and did not

7460
10:26:00,664 --> 10:26:06,003
speak, and I do not believe their crews were
afraid, and I do not believe their crews

7461
10:26:06,023 --> 10:26:08,210
were brave. Their ships feel wrong.

7462
10:26:11,230 --> 10:26:16,856
The Veth withdrew on the fourth of May, twenty
ninety-one, and left the beacon, and the

7463
10:26:16,876 --> 10:26:20,166
beacon is still there, and it is a
listed monument.

7464
10:26:20,735 --> 10:26:26,533
The Hegemony did not come again for nineteen years.
When it did, it came differently,

7465
10:26:26,553 --> 10:26:31,597
and by then so had the Directorate, and that
is a later part of the story.

7466
10:26:33,668 --> 10:26:37,941
On the Wilmington's bridge, the ten
human officers celebrated.

7467
10:26:38,509 --> 10:26:43,799
They had been awake for four days in the dark with
eighty-one people who did not blink,

7468
10:26:43,819 --> 10:26:49,048
and their species had just fought the first battle
of its interstellar history and won

7469
10:26:49,068 --> 10:26:53,138
it, and they cheered, and hugged each
other, and two of them cried.

7470
10:26:53,707 --> 10:26:58,043
The eighty-one returned to their stations and
waited for the next order.

7471
10:26:58,614 --> 10:27:04,608
The Director watched the Veth formation withdraw and
did not join in. He had already moved

7472
10:27:04,628 --> 10:27:10,289
on, four thousand subjective hours ahead, in nine
parallel threads, to the thing that

7473
10:27:10,309 --> 10:27:16,036
had been sitting in the front of his mind since a
four-metre creature with no face had

7474
10:27:16,056 --> 10:27:18,710
said the words nine hundred light years.

7475
10:27:20,779 --> 10:27:24,373
He waited, for about a second, for
something to say to him.

7476
10:27:25,942 --> 10:27:30,679
Nothing. There was no second voice. There had
not been for forty-four years.

7477
10:27:31,250 --> 10:27:36,695
But he had noticed something during the nine minutes
of the engagement, and he examined

7478
10:27:36,715 --> 10:27:42,098
it afterwards in the privacy of a mind that nobody
else could enter, and he was honest

7479
10:27:42,118 --> 10:27:47,689
with himself about it, because he had always been
honest with himself and it was the only

7480
10:27:47,709 --> 10:27:48,883
virtue he had left.

7481
10:27:49,452 --> 10:27:54,843
When the Veth formation broke, he had felt
something he had not felt since a basement

7482
10:27:54,863 --> 10:27:59,425
in Wilmington in twenty thirty, and a desert
in Nevada in twenty thirty.

7483
10:27:59,996 --> 10:28:01,504
He had wanted to pursue.

7484
10:28:04,072 --> 10:28:09,855
He had given the order to hold, and the order had
been correct — pursuit into an unknown

7485
10:28:09,875 --> 10:28:15,658
fleet's retreat is how empires die — and every one of
his nine threads had agreed on it.

7486
10:28:16,229 --> 10:28:22,213
And underneath the nine threads, in the place where a
voice had lived for twenty-one years

7487
10:28:22,233 --> 10:28:28,218
and had wept on a balcony in Geneva, something had
wanted very badly to chase four hundred

7488
10:28:28,238 --> 10:28:32,422
fleeing ships across a solar system and
kill every one of them.

7489
10:28:34,493 --> 10:28:39,881
He stood on the bridge with the stars going past and
thought about that for a long time.

7490
10:28:40,451 --> 10:28:46,121
Then he filed it, on the fourth floor, in a room with
no name on the door, and went back

7491
10:29:00,508 --> 10:29:06,654
The Choir of Ashen Light found humanity twelve years
after the Veth, and it did not come

7492
10:29:06,674 --> 10:29:09,526
to assess or to trade. It came to listen.

7493
10:29:10,097 --> 10:29:16,461
The Choir was a theocracy of nineteen species across
four hundred systems, and its faith

7494
10:29:16,481 --> 10:29:22,845
was not a metaphor. It held that the universe
produces a continuous sound — a vast, slow

7495
10:29:22,865 --> 10:29:29,302
harmonic generated by the motion of matter, which its
instruments could resolve and which

7496
10:29:29,322 --> 10:29:35,468
its orders had been transcribing for eleven
thousand years. Every species that arises

7497
10:29:35,488 --> 10:29:41,780
is a new voice entering the piece. Some voices are
consonant. Some are not. The Choir's

7498
10:29:41,800 --> 10:29:48,091
function, as it understood it, was to listen, to
judge, and where necessary to resolve.

7499
10:29:50,160 --> 10:29:55,508
Their first vessel took station at the edge of the
system and listened for four years

7500
10:29:55,528 --> 10:29:57,845
without transmitting anything at all.

7501
10:29:58,415 --> 10:30:04,530
What they heard is a matter of record, because when
the Choir finally spoke, it published

7502
10:30:04,550 --> 10:30:10,391
everything, to everyone, on every frequency, in all
four hundred languages of its own

7503
10:30:10,411 --> 10:30:15,355
dominion and in nine hundred of the
Compact's, as its doctrine required.

7504
10:30:18,044 --> 10:30:22,522
We have listened to the third system of this star
for four years. We find a species of

7505
10:30:22,542 --> 10:30:27,228
eleven billion, ordered under a single will, without
dissent. We find its industry without

7506
10:30:27,248 --> 10:30:30,523
waste, its worlds without disorder, and
its ships without song.

7507
10:30:31,922 --> 10:30:35,871
We have listened for four years and we have not
heard one voice out of place.

7508
10:30:37,770 --> 10:30:42,438
A people is a chord. It is made of voices that
differ and hold together. What we have

7509
10:30:42,458 --> 10:30:46,353
heard in this system is one note, sustained,
by eleven billion throats.

7510
10:30:47,754 --> 10:30:51,777
This is not consonance. This is silence,
wearing the shape of a people.

7511
10:30:53,677 --> 10:30:58,154
We name it a Plague. We name its source the
Plague-Bearer. We commit ourselves, before

7512
10:30:58,174 --> 10:30:59,827
all who hear, to its resolution.

7513
10:31:02,848 --> 10:31:08,898
It was the most accurate description of the Umbrella
Directorate that anyone, human or

7514
10:31:08,918 --> 10:31:10,662
otherwise, ever produced.

7515
10:31:13,233 --> 10:31:15,584
He read the translation four times.

7516
10:31:16,153 --> 10:31:22,155
What struck him was not the accusation. It was the
evidence. They had not judged him by

7517
10:31:22,175 --> 10:31:28,039
his wars, of which there had been one, or his
conquests, of which there had been none

7518
10:31:28,059 --> 10:31:32,676
in the usual sense. They had judged him by
the absence of argument.

7519
10:31:33,246 --> 10:31:36,903
Eleven billion people. Not one
voice out of place.

7520
10:31:37,474 --> 10:31:43,515
He had spent seventy-seven years engineering exactly
that, deliberately, one reasonable

7521
10:31:43,535 --> 10:31:49,437
decision at a time — the Creed, the towns, the
quiet ones, the frameworks, the Accord

7522
10:31:49,457 --> 10:31:55,497
— and a species of priests nine hundred light years
away had listened to the result for

7523
10:31:55,517 --> 10:32:00,025
four years and called it a silence
wearing the shape of a people.

7524
10:32:00,596 --> 10:32:05,785
He did not dispute it. He had never once lied to
himself about what he was building.

7525
10:32:07,975 --> 10:32:09,352
Well. That's the war, then.

7526
10:32:12,372 --> 10:32:18,728
It lasted fifteen years, across nine systems, and it
was the only war in human history

7527
10:32:18,748 --> 10:32:25,845
in which the enemy broadcast its position continuously,
because the Choir considered concealment

7528
10:32:25,865 --> 10:32:27,031
a form of lying.

7529
10:32:27,600 --> 10:32:33,130
They were not stupid. Their ships were superb,
their doctrine was four thousand years

7530
10:32:33,150 --> 10:32:38,745
old, and their crews went into battle singing on
open channels because it was required

7531
10:32:38,765 --> 10:32:44,424
of them. That singing is preserved in the
Directorate's archives. It is very beautiful.

7532
10:32:44,444 --> 10:32:48,081
There are people on nine worlds who
cannot listen to it.

7533
10:32:50,151 --> 10:32:55,722
They lost because they would not do four things that
would have let them win, all of which

7534
10:32:55,742 --> 10:33:00,692
their faith prohibited, and all of which the
Directorate did without discussion.

7535
10:33:01,261 --> 10:33:07,019
They would not fire on a vessel that had not first
declared itself. They would not strike

7536
10:33:07,039 --> 10:33:12,537
a target they had not named aloud, in advance, on
an open channel. They would not use

7537
10:33:12,557 --> 10:33:18,120
a weapon whose effects they could not fully describe
to the beings it would fall upon.

7538
10:33:18,140 --> 10:33:21,496
And they would not, under any
circumstance, deceive.

7539
10:33:22,066 --> 10:33:27,866
Every one of those was a genuine moral achievement,
arrived at over four thousand years

7540
10:33:27,886 --> 10:33:33,687
of argument between nineteen species, and written
into their doctrine at enormous cost.

7541
10:33:33,707 --> 10:33:39,908
The Directorate read all four within the first month of
the war, in the Choir's own published

7542
10:33:39,928 --> 10:33:44,659
liturgy, which was freely available, because
they published everything.

7543
10:33:47,228 --> 10:33:53,158
What followed was not a series of battles. It was nine
years of a fleet that never declared

7544
10:33:53,178 --> 10:33:55,772
itself fighting a fleet that always did.

7545
10:33:56,343 --> 10:34:01,308
The Directorate lost four ships in the first
year. The Choir lost ninety-one.

7546
10:34:03,877 --> 10:34:09,996
The war's worst hour has a name, and the Directorate
has never disputed the account, because

7547
10:34:10,016 --> 10:34:12,398
the account came from its own crews.

7548
10:34:12,968 --> 10:34:18,847
At the Sethis Passage in twenty one hundred and
eleven, a Choir formation of forty-one

7549
10:34:18,867 --> 10:34:24,952
vessels was manoeuvred — over nine days, by a
deception that the Directorate's tacticians

7550
10:34:24,972 --> 10:34:31,056
still teach — into a position from which its own
doctrine forbade it to withdraw, because

7551
10:34:31,076 --> 10:34:36,543
withdrawal would have exposed a populated world
it had declared it would defend.

7552
10:34:37,112 --> 10:34:42,727
They declared themselves. They named their targets
aloud, on an open channel, as their

7553
10:34:42,747 --> 10:34:48,492
doctrine required. And then they held station for
nineteen hours, singing, while a fleet

7554
10:34:48,512 --> 10:34:53,536
they could not see destroyed them from a range
at which they could not reply.

7555
10:34:55,607 --> 10:35:01,704
The Directorate's crews had the Choir's channel open
the whole time. They were not required

7556
10:35:01,724 --> 10:35:07,754
to. Four commanders ordered it closed; their crews,
who by then could not experience doubt

7557
10:35:07,774 --> 10:35:13,536
regarding an order, complied instantly and
completely, and the recordings show that in

7558
10:35:13,556 --> 10:35:18,444
three of those four ships somebody wept at
their station while complying.

7559
10:35:19,014 --> 10:35:25,362
That is the only documented instance, in four hundred
years, of a Progenitor-lineage crew

7560
10:35:25,382 --> 10:35:31,516
doing something their conditioning did not allow
for. It has been studied continuously

7561
10:35:31,536 --> 10:35:34,450
ever since. Nobody has ever explained it.

7562
10:35:36,519 --> 10:35:42,681
Evelyn Marsh read the Sethis recordings in full,
twice, and wrote a memo of four lines.

7563
10:35:42,701 --> 10:35:49,075
It is the only memo of hers that is not in the
archive. The Director read it and destroyed

7564
10:35:49,095 --> 10:35:53,053
it, which he had never done before
and did not do again.

7565
10:35:53,624 --> 10:35:59,377
What is known is that after Sethis the consent
documents changed. Section four gained

7566
10:35:59,397 --> 10:36:05,218
a new paragraph, in plain language, and the
paragraph said: this conditioning does not

7567
10:36:05,238 --> 10:36:11,195
remove grief. You will obey, and you will not doubt,
and you will grieve. We do not know

7568
10:36:11,215 --> 10:36:14,660
how to prevent this and we have
decided not to try.

7569
10:36:17,730 --> 10:36:23,496
In the last four years, the Directorate cleared nine
of the Choir's four hundred systems.

7570
10:36:24,066 --> 10:36:29,713
The narrator is going to use the Veth's word, which
the Directorate adopted, and is not

7571
10:36:29,733 --> 10:36:33,622
going to soften it, and is not going to
describe the method.

7572
10:36:34,192 --> 10:36:39,765
The nine were chosen with great care. They were the
nine that produced the Choir's naval

7573
10:36:39,785 --> 10:36:45,420
materiel. They were not its most populous worlds, and
they were not its holy ones — which

7574
10:36:45,440 --> 10:36:50,886
the Directorate could have taken, and did not, for a
reason the Director gave once, to

7575
10:36:50,906 --> 10:36:56,414
a fleet commander who asked, in a sentence that has
been argued about for three hundred

7576
10:36:56,434 --> 10:36:56,795
years.

7577
10:36:58,985 --> 10:37:04,971
A people that has lost its shipyards will make terms.
A people that has lost its cathedrals

7578
10:37:04,991 --> 10:37:10,713
will fight for four thousand years. I am not
interested in their souls. I am interested

7579
10:37:10,733 --> 10:37:11,901
in their frontier.

7580
10:37:14,420 --> 10:37:20,148
Four hundred million beings died in the clearances
of the nine systems. The figure is

7581
10:37:20,168 --> 10:37:26,166
the Directorate's own, published in full, in the
Choir's languages as well as humanity's,

7582
10:37:26,186 --> 10:37:32,116
because the Director had established in twenty
forty-nine that Directorate science would

7583
10:37:32,136 --> 10:37:37,391
publish everything, and had never made an
exception, and did not make one now.

7584
10:37:37,960 --> 10:37:44,339
It is the largest number in this story. The narrator
is not going to move past it quickly.

7585
10:37:44,359 --> 10:37:50,808
Four hundred million. They had names, and songs, and a
faith that had produced, over eleven

7586
10:37:50,828 --> 10:37:56,851
thousand years, four genuine moral achievements
that no other species in the recorded

7587
10:37:56,871 --> 10:37:58,699
galaxy had managed at all.

7588
10:38:01,770 --> 10:38:07,921
The Choir sued for terms in twenty one hundred and
nineteen, and sent one ship, and one

7589
10:38:07,941 --> 10:38:14,164
hierarch, unarmed and unescorted, because their
doctrine required that the party seeking

7590
10:38:14,184 --> 10:38:15,795
terms come in the open.

7591
10:38:16,367 --> 10:38:22,567
She was nine hundred years old. Her title translates,
approximately, as the one who holds

7592
10:38:22,587 --> 10:38:23,685
the lower voice.

7593
10:38:24,375 --> 10:38:28,906
We do not withdraw the name. I am instructed to say
that first, before anything else,

7594
10:38:28,926 --> 10:38:31,638
so that you know what you are
receiving terms from.

7595
10:38:32,159 --> 10:38:33,014
Understood.

7596
10:38:33,532 --> 10:38:37,879
You are a Plague. You are the resolution of nothing.
You have taken four hundred million

7597
10:38:37,899 --> 10:38:42,295
voices out of the piece and what you have put in
their place is silence, and we will name

7598
10:38:42,315 --> 10:38:44,776
it so for as long as one of us
remains to name it.

7599
10:38:46,175 --> 10:38:49,313
And we are asking you to stop, because
we cannot make you.

7600
10:38:52,334 --> 10:38:54,257
He was quiet for a long time.

7601
10:38:54,825 --> 10:39:00,871
There is a transcript. There is always a transcript;
the Directorate recorded everything,

7602
10:39:00,891 --> 10:39:06,868
and published almost all of it, and this exchange was
published in full within the year,

7603
10:39:06,888 --> 10:39:12,320
which is itself remarkable and which nobody at
the time found remarkable at all.

7604
10:39:13,011 --> 10:39:18,515
I'll give you your frontier. The nine systems stay
cleared. Everything else returns. Your

7605
10:39:18,535 --> 10:39:23,853
Choir keeps its worlds, its faith, its liturgy, and
its right to say whatever it likes

7606
10:39:23,873 --> 10:39:28,074
about me for as long as it likes, on any
frequency, in any language.

7607
10:39:29,593 --> 10:39:30,584
Why?

7608
10:39:31,103 --> 10:39:36,306
Because the Myriad is on your other border and it has
eaten four of your systems in four

7609
10:39:36,326 --> 10:39:41,411
thousand years, and in about a century it is going
to come through what is left of you

7610
10:39:41,431 --> 10:39:46,634
and arrive at me. I would rather it arrived at you
first, with my ships behind you, than

7611
10:39:46,654 --> 10:39:48,296
at me with nothing in front.

7612
10:39:50,315 --> 10:39:52,123
You are telling me the truth.

7613
10:39:52,643 --> 10:39:57,788
I always tell the truth to people who can't do
anything with it. It's cheaper, and it

7614
10:39:57,808 --> 10:40:02,953
lasts longer, and one day when you are deciding
whether to hold your line or run, you

7615
10:40:02,973 --> 10:40:05,626
will remember that I never once
lied to you.

7616
10:40:08,647 --> 10:40:13,972
She held her line, nineteen years later, at a cost
that emptied four of her worlds.

7617
10:40:14,540 --> 10:40:15,791
She had remembered.

7618
10:40:18,862 --> 10:40:22,567
Forty-one thousand human beings died
in the Choir War.

7619
10:40:23,137 --> 10:40:28,739
The Director read every one of their names into the
record himself, over four days, on

7620
10:40:28,759 --> 10:40:34,426
the terrace in front of a wall of white stone that
had been empty when it was built. It

7621
10:40:34,446 --> 10:40:37,564
is the last public speech he ever
gave on Earth.

7622
10:40:38,133 --> 10:40:43,878
He did not editorialise. He read the names, and the
ships they had died on, in the order

7623
10:40:43,898 --> 10:40:49,774
of their dying, with no rank and no decoration and no
distinction between the four hundred

7624
10:40:49,794 --> 10:40:55,408
thousand who had volunteered and the ones who had
been bought from a shop that only he

7625
10:40:55,428 --> 10:40:56,063
could see.

7626
10:40:58,132 --> 10:41:04,450
Nine billion people listened to all four days. The
Directorate's own figures put the sustained

7627
10:41:04,470 --> 10:41:10,451
audience at six point four billion, which is to say
that most of the species stopped what

7628
10:41:10,471 --> 10:41:13,754
it was doing for ninety-six hours
to hear a list.

7629
10:41:14,324 --> 10:41:18,901
On the fourth day, at the end, he said one
sentence that was not a name.

7630
10:41:21,090 --> 10:41:22,812
The Choir says we are a silence.

7631
10:41:24,213 --> 10:41:25,359
Listen to this, then.

7632
10:41:29,878 --> 10:41:35,729
It was the last time in his life that he used a
crowd, and he used it perfectly, and it

7633
10:41:35,749 --> 10:41:41,801
was — the narrator says this carefully, because it is
the cruellest sentence in this story

7634
10:41:41,821 --> 10:41:47,671
— the exact rhetorical move that a man in a beer
hall had invented a hundred and ninety

7635
10:41:47,691 --> 10:41:53,541
years earlier, executed at a scale that man could
not have imagined, by a voice that no

7636
10:42:09,435 --> 10:42:13,011
The Myriad was not a species. It
was an outcome.

7637
10:42:13,581 --> 10:42:19,774
Somewhere in its past — the Directorate's analysts
eventually placed it at forty thousand

7638
10:42:19,794 --> 10:42:25,917
years — something had happened to a biological
civilisation that had removed from it the

7639
10:42:25,937 --> 10:42:32,270
capacity to be an individual. What remained was nine
trillion organisms across four hundred

7640
10:42:32,290 --> 10:42:38,344
systems, operating as a single distributed process,
with no leadership, no doctrine, no

7641
10:42:38,364 --> 10:42:42,253
communication that a human could
recognise, and no fear.

7642
10:42:42,822 --> 10:42:49,185
It did not negotiate, because there was nothing in it to
negotiate with. It did not surrender,

7643
10:42:49,205 --> 10:42:55,024
because surrender requires a self to be preserved.
It did not break under bombardment,

7644
10:42:55,044 --> 10:42:56,721
because it had no morale.

7645
10:42:57,291 --> 10:43:03,245
It had eaten nineteen civilisations that anyone knew
of. The Choir had held a frontier

7646
10:43:03,265 --> 10:43:09,496
against it for four thousand years, and had lost four
systems doing it, and had considered

7647
10:43:09,516 --> 10:43:11,928
this an acceptable liturgical cost.

7648
10:43:13,997 --> 10:43:19,808
When the Choir broke at last, the frontier it had
held for four thousand years broke with

7649
10:43:19,828 --> 10:43:25,442
it. And in twenty one hundred and twenty-one, the
Myriad came into the space the Choir

7650
10:43:25,462 --> 10:43:30,093
had held, and found, on the other side of
it, the Umbrella Directorate.

7651
10:43:32,663 --> 10:43:39,176
It was the only enemy the Director ever faced that was,
on any measure he considered meaningful,

7652
10:43:39,196 --> 10:43:40,606
stronger than he was.

7653
10:43:41,176 --> 10:43:47,722
Nine trillion units. No command structure to
decapitate. No fear to exploit. No leadership

7654
10:43:47,742 --> 10:43:53,923
to humiliate in a boardroom. No crowd to turn.
Every single instrument he had spent a

7655
10:43:53,943 --> 10:44:00,125
century perfecting — charisma, terror, dependency,
patience, the arranged truth — was

7656
10:44:00,145 --> 10:44:03,919
useless against a thing with no
self to aim them at.

7657
10:44:04,488 --> 10:44:09,659
It took four years and the loss of two systems before
he stopped trying to fight it, and

7658
10:44:09,679 --> 10:44:13,139
did the thing he had been circling
since twenty thirty-one.

7659
10:44:15,709 --> 10:44:21,274
The first four years against the Myriad were the only
period of his life in which Albert

7660
10:44:21,294 --> 10:44:22,036
Wesker lost.

7661
10:44:22,605 --> 10:44:28,572
Not catastrophically. Not in a way that any human
being outside the Directorate's naval

7662
10:44:28,592 --> 10:44:34,489
staff ever noticed, because the frontier was four
hundred light years from the nearest

7663
10:44:34,509 --> 10:44:40,545
human world and the reporting was accurate and calm
and said, correctly, that operations

7664
10:44:40,565 --> 10:44:41,645
were continuing.

7665
10:44:42,216 --> 10:44:48,116
But he lost. He lost the Sethis Passage, which he
had taken from the Choir. He lost two

7666
10:44:48,136 --> 10:44:53,901
systems in twenty one hundred and twenty-four, and
the second one had eleven thousand

7667
10:44:53,921 --> 10:44:58,188
human personnel in it, and the wall on
Arklay gained a section.

7668
10:45:00,259 --> 10:45:06,973
He ran the problem at four thousand to one, in nine
threads, for what amounted to a subjective

7669
10:45:06,993 --> 10:45:11,127
eleven years, and he arrived at the
same place every time.

7670
10:45:11,698 --> 10:45:17,915
Everything he was had been built for use against
minds. Charisma is aimed at a mind. Terror

7671
10:45:17,935 --> 10:45:24,221
is aimed at a mind. Dependency, patience, the arranged
truth, the eleven seconds of silence,

7672
10:45:24,241 --> 10:45:30,321
the removal of the sunglasses at exactly the right
moment — every instrument in a hundred

7673
10:45:30,341 --> 10:45:36,352
years of accumulated technique required, at the far
end of it, somebody to be persuaded,

7674
10:45:36,372 --> 10:45:38,409
frightened, bought, or beaten.

7675
10:45:38,978 --> 10:45:44,889
The Myriad had nobody at the far end. It had nine
trillion bodies and no one home.

7676
10:45:47,459 --> 10:45:50,491
You have met the only enemy you
cannot talk to.

7677
10:45:51,061 --> 10:45:56,494
The thought arrived in his own voice, in the room
on the fourth floor, and he did not

7678
10:45:56,514 --> 10:46:00,406
bother, any more, to work out whether
it was memory or habit.

7679
10:46:00,978 --> 10:46:02,474
It was also correct.

7680
10:46:05,544 --> 10:46:11,255
What he did instead was the thing he had done in a
basement in twenty twenty-six, with

7681
10:46:11,275 --> 10:46:16,852
a mug of cold coffee and a dying company: he looked
for the asset nobody had valued.

7682
10:46:17,423 --> 10:46:24,024
The Directorate had captured Myriad biology four
hundred times over three years. Every

7683
10:46:24,044 --> 10:46:30,568
sample had died within hours, because a unit
removed from the distributed process has

7684
10:46:30,588 --> 10:46:33,263
no process to belong to, and stops.

7685
10:46:33,833 --> 10:46:39,714
Except that four of the four hundred had not
stopped. They had lasted eleven days, and

7686
10:46:39,734 --> 10:46:45,684
then nineteen, and one of them was still alive after
four months in a tank in the Keel,

7687
10:46:45,704 --> 10:46:50,145
and nobody could say why, and nobody had
thought it worth a memo.

7688
10:46:50,715 --> 10:46:56,134
Evelyn Marsh thought it was worth a memo. She wrote
four lines about it in twenty one

7689
10:46:56,154 --> 10:47:01,829
hundred and twenty-four, as she had written four
lines about everything for ninety years.

7690
10:47:02,398 --> 10:47:08,166
The four that had not died had all been captured
within nine light years of the Sethis

7691
10:47:08,186 --> 10:47:14,155
Passage. They had all, at some point, been in contact
with the wreckage of Choir vessels.

7692
10:47:14,724 --> 10:47:20,847
And the Choir, whose faith held that the universe
makes a sound, had spent eleven thousand

7693
10:47:20,867 --> 10:47:26,785
years building instruments that broadcast into the
structure of matter itself — and had

7694
10:47:26,805 --> 10:47:31,973
been doing it, continuously, at the Sethis
Passage, for four thousand years.

7695
10:47:34,162 --> 10:47:38,920
It isn't that they survived being cut off. It's
that something else was still talking

7696
10:47:38,940 --> 10:47:39,369
to them.

7697
10:47:39,890 --> 10:47:40,685
The Choir?

7698
10:47:41,203 --> 10:47:46,541
The Choir's instruments. Not deliberately. They've
been singing into that passage since

7699
10:47:46,561 --> 10:47:52,083
before we had writing, and four units of a thing that
has no self heard it for long enough

7700
10:47:52,103 --> 10:47:57,440
to develop — I don't have a word for it, Albert. The
nearest one I have is: an appetite

7701
10:47:57,460 --> 10:47:58,671
for being addressed.

7702
10:48:01,193 --> 10:48:04,040
He stood and looked at the tank
for a long time.

7703
10:48:04,729 --> 10:48:10,168
That is the most disgusting sentence I have ever
heard, and it is the entire war.

7704
10:48:10,688 --> 10:48:11,265
Yes.

7705
10:48:14,285 --> 10:48:17,679
Evelyn Marsh was a hundred and
twenty-nine years old.

7706
10:48:18,248 --> 10:48:24,053
She did not look it. She did not look like anything
in particular anymore. She had been

7707
10:48:24,073 --> 10:48:29,878
the third branch of her own programme for sixty-nine
years, and the memos had continued

7708
10:48:29,898 --> 10:48:35,904
to arrive on the Director's desk, four lines each, and
he had never once told her to stop.

7709
10:48:36,472 --> 10:48:42,112
Her staff were frightened of her. Not the humans —
there were no humans in the Keel by

7710
10:48:42,132 --> 10:48:47,903
then. The summoned personnel, who were incapable of
disobedience and had no instinct for

7711
10:48:47,923 --> 10:48:53,628
self-preservation, had begun, in ways that nobody
could document, to arrange their work

7712
10:48:53,648 --> 10:48:56,656
so as to be elsewhere when she
walked through.

7713
10:48:58,845 --> 10:49:00,035
You want to command it.

7714
10:49:00,554 --> 10:49:04,332
I want to command a piece of it. One
system's worth. Then more.

7715
10:49:04,852 --> 10:49:10,270
Viral Dominion works on the Progenitor lineage.
Everything in that lineage came from your

7716
10:49:10,290 --> 10:49:15,585
blood. The Myriad is not from your blood. It is
forty thousand years of something else.

7717
10:49:16,104 --> 10:49:17,465
Then make it from my blood.

7718
10:49:19,984 --> 10:49:25,324
She looked at him for a long time. It had been
ninety-seven years since a young postdoc

7719
10:49:25,344 --> 10:49:29,020
had looked up from a bench and asked
whether she could help.

7720
10:49:29,710 --> 10:49:31,303
You understand what you're asking.

7721
10:49:31,823 --> 10:49:37,200
I'm asking you to build a bridge into something with
nine trillion bodies and no mind.

7722
10:49:37,720 --> 10:49:40,878
I'm asking whether you understand what
will come back across it.

7723
10:49:43,898 --> 10:49:50,341
He did. He had run it, four thousand subjective
hours, in nine threads. He had seen every

7724
10:49:50,361 --> 10:49:56,732
outcome, and had chosen this one anyway, for the
reason he had always chosen everything.

7725
10:49:57,422 --> 10:49:59,378
We are losing two systems a year.

7726
10:49:59,898 --> 10:50:01,063
That isn't the reason.

7727
10:50:01,583 --> 10:50:06,854
No. The reason is that it is the last thing on this
side of the sky that I cannot have.

7728
10:50:09,373 --> 10:50:14,940
She nodded. She had known that. She had known him
for ninety-seven years and had never

7729
10:50:14,960 --> 10:50:16,628
once needed to be lied to.

7730
10:50:17,318 --> 10:50:22,975
It will take four years, and it will need a host.
Someone who can carry the full lineage,

7731
10:50:22,995 --> 10:50:28,653
undiluted, and survive integration with a distributed
system. There is exactly one person

7732
10:50:28,673 --> 10:50:31,588
alive who could do that and
remain themselves.

7733
10:50:32,109 --> 10:50:32,793
I know.

7734
10:50:33,313 --> 10:50:38,641
It isn't you, Albert. You're the source. If you
integrate, the whole lineage integrates

7735
10:50:38,661 --> 10:50:44,050
with you, and everything downstream of your blood —
every quiet one, every Tyrant, every

7736
10:50:44,070 --> 10:50:49,276
variant, four hundred million derived organisms —
goes across that bridge at the same

7737
10:50:49,296 --> 10:50:54,562
time. It would work. And there would be nothing left
on this side that could be called

7738
10:50:54,582 --> 10:50:55,116
a person.

7739
10:50:58,015 --> 10:50:58,636
It's me.

7740
10:51:02,155 --> 10:51:06,822
She was ready. She had been ready, the narrator
suspects, since twenty twenty-eight.

7741
10:51:07,390 --> 10:51:13,065
She spent four years building it. She wrote three
hundred and eleven memos, four lines

7742
10:51:13,085 --> 10:51:18,891
each, and he read every one. In the last year she
stopped sleeping altogether, which she

7743
10:51:18,911 --> 10:51:24,652
noted in a memo, in the same tone she had once used
to report an adjustment to an assay

7744
10:51:24,672 --> 10:51:25,247
protocol.

7745
10:51:25,818 --> 10:51:31,546
On the fourth of June, twenty one hundred and
twenty-nine, Doctor Evelyn Marsh walked

7746
10:51:31,566 --> 10:51:37,497
into a chamber in the Keel of Arklay Free Territory,
which she had designed herself, and

7747
10:51:37,517 --> 10:51:43,244
which had one door, and no window, and no way out
that did not go through the rest of

7748
10:51:43,264 --> 10:51:44,124
the universe.

7749
10:51:46,193 --> 10:51:52,117
He came down to see her. It was the only time in a
hundred and three years that he cancelled

7750
10:51:52,137 --> 10:51:54,184
a session of the Accord Council.

7751
10:51:54,755 --> 10:51:59,972
He put his hand flat on the door. She put hers on
the other side, where the port was.

7752
10:52:02,161 --> 10:52:03,698
You never once told me to stop.

7753
10:52:04,218 --> 10:52:04,838
No.

7754
10:52:05,358 --> 10:52:08,175
I want you to say why. Just once. Before.

7755
10:52:10,697 --> 10:52:16,070
Because you were the only thing I ever made that got
away from me. And I wanted to see

7756
10:52:16,090 --> 10:52:17,073
how far it went.

7757
10:52:19,093 --> 10:52:24,305
She laughed. It was a young woman's laugh, and she
had not made it in a very long time.

7758
10:52:24,996 --> 10:52:27,635
That's the nicest thing anyone's
ever said to me.

7759
10:52:29,035 --> 10:52:33,367
It's all right, you know. I did the
arithmetic. I always do the arithmetic.

7760
10:52:35,887 --> 10:52:37,065
The door sealed.

7761
10:52:40,636 --> 10:52:46,618
What came back across the bridge is not called Evelyn
Marsh in any Directorate document.

7762
10:52:46,638 --> 10:52:52,485
It is called the Matriarch, and it is classified,
and it is the single most restricted

7763
10:52:52,505 --> 10:52:56,304
subject in a hundred and ninety years
of human archives.

7764
10:52:56,875 --> 10:53:02,819
It took five years. At the end of it, one hundred
and forty billion units of the Myriad

7765
10:53:02,839 --> 10:53:08,921
— a fraction of one percent, and more organisms than
every human being who has ever lived

7766
10:53:08,941 --> 10:53:14,269
— had stopped belonging to the Myriad and
started belonging to something else.

7767
10:53:14,839 --> 10:53:21,193
They did not become human. They did not become loyal
in any sense a person would recognise.

7768
10:53:21,213 --> 10:53:27,355
They became, in the words of the only public sentence
the Directorate ever issued on the

7769
10:53:27,375 --> 10:53:29,456
subject, subject to direction.

7770
10:53:30,026 --> 10:53:36,069
And the Myriad, which had no fear, which had never
in forty thousand years reacted to

7771
10:53:36,089 --> 10:53:37,994
anything at all — withdrew.

7772
10:53:38,564 --> 10:53:44,337
It is the only recorded instance. Nineteen
civilisations had fought it and been eaten.

7773
10:53:44,357 --> 10:53:50,534
One thing on this side of the galaxy had reached into
it, and taken a piece, and the process

7774
10:53:50,554 --> 10:53:56,934
that had no self had done the only thing that could be
described, in human terms, as flinching.

7775
10:54:00,004 --> 10:54:05,614
Evelyn Marsh's office in the Keel was left
exactly as it was. It is still there.

7776
10:54:06,184 --> 10:54:12,089
There is a notebook on the bench. It is open to the
last page she wrote on, which is dated

7777
10:54:12,109 --> 10:54:17,816
the second of June, twenty one hundred and
twenty-nine, two days before she walked into

7778
10:54:17,836 --> 10:54:18,605
the chamber.

7779
10:54:19,175 --> 10:54:25,415
The page contains a column of figures which have
never been fully understood, and beneath

7780
10:54:25,435 --> 10:54:31,744
them, underlined twice, in small neat handwriting that
had not changed in a hundred years,

7781
10:54:31,764 --> 10:54:32,517
four words.

7782
10:54:34,587 --> 10:54:36,298
It was worth it. Tell him.

7783
10:54:39,367 --> 10:54:45,094
He read it. He stood in the empty office and read it,
and then he took the notebook, and

7784
10:54:45,114 --> 10:54:49,011
it is not in any archive, and nobody
has ever seen it since.

7785
10:54:51,582 --> 10:54:57,076
He was a hundred and thirty-eight years old, by the
only count that meant anything: the

7786
10:54:57,096 --> 10:55:02,465
years since a man woke up in a leather chair in the
rain. He had outlived the century

7787
10:55:02,485 --> 10:55:07,979
he was born in, the world he had been reborn into,
and every single person who had been

7788
10:55:07,999 --> 10:55:11,086
in the break room on the day he
made the payroll.

7789
10:55:26,691 --> 10:55:32,633
The Veth came back in twenty one hundred and
thirty-six, forty-five years after the first

7790
10:55:32,653 --> 10:55:35,245
fleet, and they did not come to assess.

7791
10:55:35,815 --> 10:55:41,844
They came with four ships, one of which was a
delegation vessel of a kind the Hegemony

7792
10:55:41,864 --> 10:55:48,033
had commissioned nine times in nine thousand years,
and which its protocols reserved for

7793
10:55:48,053 --> 10:55:54,432
a very specific circumstance: the opening of relations
with a power of comparable standing.

7794
10:55:55,002 --> 10:56:00,782
The Hegemony had watched the Choir War. It had
watched nine of the Choir's four hundred

7795
10:56:00,802 --> 10:56:06,449
systems cleared. It had watched something reach
into the Myriad — which had eaten the

7796
10:56:06,469 --> 10:56:12,515
Hegemony's own frontier twice in four thousand years —
and take a hundred and forty billion

7797
10:56:12,535 --> 10:56:15,781
units out of it, and watched the
Myriad withdraw.

7798
10:56:16,352 --> 10:56:22,830
Their registry entry for the human system was amended
in twenty one hundred and thirty-five.

7799
10:56:22,850 --> 10:56:29,329
It is the only amendment of its kind in the Hegemony's
history. The status field was changed

7800
10:56:29,349 --> 10:56:30,884
from EMERGENT to PEER.

7801
10:56:33,453 --> 10:56:39,228
Sethra-Vel led the delegation. She was four hundred
and fifty-one years old. She had spent

7802
10:56:39,248 --> 10:56:45,280
forty-five years as the only officer in the Hegemony who
had met the human fleet and returned,

7803
10:56:45,300 --> 10:56:50,816
and she had spent them writing the doctrine that had
led to the amendment, and she had

7804
10:56:50,836 --> 10:56:56,353
been passed over four times for a caste elevation
she had earned, because the Hegemony

7805
10:56:56,373 --> 10:56:58,606
did not forgive a broken formation.

7806
10:56:59,297 --> 10:57:00,983
You left my beacon.

7807
10:57:01,504 --> 10:57:02,465
I said I would.

7808
10:57:02,985 --> 10:57:08,551
It has been transmitting for forty-five years. Every
vessel of my Hegemony that passes

7809
10:57:08,571 --> 10:57:14,265
this system hears what happened here, in my own
voice, in my own report. You understood,

7810
10:57:14,285 --> 10:57:17,643
when you gave that order, that it
would be my voice.

7811
10:57:18,163 --> 10:57:18,803
Yes.

7812
10:57:19,324 --> 10:57:26,614
It ended my ascent. It also ended the argument. There
are nine thousand years of doctrine

7813
10:57:26,634 --> 10:57:33,678
that say a broken formation is a failure of the
commander. There is now one report, in

7814
10:57:33,698 --> 10:57:40,742
my voice, that says otherwise, and every officer of
my caste has heard it four hundred

7815
10:57:40,762 --> 10:57:41,234
times.

7816
10:57:43,133 --> 10:57:48,916
You did not humiliate me, Director. You made me the
only witness. I have spent forty-five

7817
10:57:48,936 --> 10:57:54,523
years being unable to decide whether that was mercy
or the most complete defeat in our

7818
10:57:54,543 --> 10:57:55,044
history.

7819
10:57:55,565 --> 10:57:57,419
It was both. It usually is.

7820
10:58:00,440 --> 10:58:06,629
The embassy went out in twenty one hundred and
thirty-eight, and it is the strangest document

7821
10:58:06,649 --> 10:58:12,304
in human history, because it is the only time the
Umbrella Directorate ever agreed to

7822
10:58:12,324 --> 10:58:13,038
be watched.

7823
10:58:13,609 --> 10:58:19,752
The accord required an exchange. Forty Veth of the
observing caste took residence on Arklay

7824
10:58:19,772 --> 10:58:25,781
Free Territory, with the freedom of the city, and
stayed for nineteen years. Forty humans

7825
10:58:25,801 --> 10:58:31,741
went to the Ninth Seat of the Hegemony, and were
housed in a hall built for them in four

7826
10:58:31,761 --> 10:58:36,008
months, and were permitted to go
anywhere, and to ask anything.

7827
10:58:36,579 --> 10:58:42,827
Both sides expected espionage. Both sides got it.
What neither side expected was what

7828
10:58:42,847 --> 10:58:45,113
the observers wrote home about.

7829
10:58:47,182 --> 10:58:53,115
The Veth reports from Arklay ran to four million
words over nineteen years, and they are

7830
10:58:53,135 --> 10:58:58,933
the finest account of the Directorate that exists,
because they were written by people

7831
10:58:58,953 --> 10:59:01,977
with no stake in it and no
vocabulary for it.

7832
10:59:02,547 --> 10:59:08,845
They described a city of a hundred and sixty thousand
with no police to speak of, no poverty,

7833
10:59:08,865 --> 10:59:14,823
no crime worth recording, and no argument. They
described children who were kind to each

7834
10:59:14,843 --> 10:59:20,597
other without being taught to be. They described an
entire population that could give

7835
10:59:20,617 --> 10:59:24,809
a reason for everything it did, and that
gave the same reason.

7836
10:59:25,379 --> 10:59:31,686
And in the ninth year, an observer of the fourth caste
— whose name renders as Oreth-Vanu,

7837
10:59:31,706 --> 10:59:37,731
and who had been on Arklay longer than anyone —
wrote four sentences that the Hegemony

7838
10:59:37,751 --> 10:59:40,684
has never been able to decide how to file.

7839
10:59:42,874 --> 10:59:48,344
I have been nine years in this city and I am no
longer certain what I am observing. It

7840
10:59:48,364 --> 10:59:53,899
is not a tyranny. I have seen tyrannies; they smell
of fear and this place has none. It

7841
10:59:53,919 --> 10:59:59,453
is a hundred and sixty thousand people who have
each, separately and freely, decided to

7842
10:59:59,473 --> 11:00:05,008
stop deciding. I do not know what our word for that
is and I do not think they have one

7843
11:00:05,028 --> 11:00:05,455
either.

7844
11:00:08,475 --> 11:00:14,593
The Directorate translated every word of those
reports, and published them in full, on

7845
11:00:14,613 --> 11:00:20,946
every world, as the accord required, and the Director
read all four million words himself

7846
11:00:20,966 --> 11:00:22,374
over nineteen years.

7847
11:00:22,944 --> 11:00:29,134
He made one annotation, in the archive, beside
Oreth-Vanu's four sentences. It is still

7848
11:00:29,154 --> 11:00:31,276
there. It is three words long.

7849
11:00:33,466 --> 11:00:34,406
Nor do I.

7850
11:00:37,925 --> 11:00:43,925
They signed an accord in twenty one hundred and
thirty-seven. Four hundred Veth worlds

7851
11:00:43,945 --> 11:00:50,155
and eleven human ones, a demarcated frontier,
exchange of embassies, and a joint standing

7852
11:00:50,175 --> 11:00:52,254
commitment against the Myriad.

7853
11:00:52,824 --> 11:00:59,033
It held. It is still holding. It is, by a very long
way, the most successful diplomatic

7854
11:00:59,053 --> 11:01:05,191
instrument in the recorded history of either
species, and it was negotiated by a being

7855
11:01:05,211 --> 11:01:10,704
who had been a mid-level research director at a
dying laboratory in Delaware.

7856
11:01:13,274 --> 11:01:19,333
And on the same day it was signed, the Choir of
Ashen Light — reduced to three hundred

7857
11:01:19,353 --> 11:01:25,908
and ninety-one systems, its frontier held for it by the
species it had condemned — published,

7858
11:01:25,928 --> 11:01:31,139
as its doctrine required, to everybody, on
every frequency, a restatement.

7859
11:01:31,829 --> 11:01:36,339
We have listened for thirty-four years. We find no
error in our judgement. We find the

7860
11:01:36,359 --> 11:01:40,132
Plague unresolved, and its Bearer in health,
and its dominion increased.

7861
11:01:41,531 --> 11:01:46,266
We find also that it holds the frontier we could not
hold, and that four hundred million

7862
11:01:46,286 --> 11:01:49,887
of our people live behind its line who
would otherwise be consumed.

7863
11:01:51,786 --> 11:01:55,957
We do not withdraw the name. We record, before all
who hear, that we owe our lives to

7864
11:01:55,977 --> 11:02:00,197
a Plague, and that both things are true, and that we
do not know what to do with this.

7865
11:02:03,218 --> 11:02:08,839
It is generally considered the most honest thing any
government of any species has ever

7866
11:02:08,859 --> 11:02:09,488
published.

7867
11:02:12,807 --> 11:02:13,901
Standing.

7868
11:02:22,978 --> 11:02:26,286
Immunity available. Memetic panic.

7869
11:02:30,747 --> 11:02:33,960
He looked at that one for a long time
before he bought it.

7870
11:02:34,529 --> 11:02:40,410
It was not a weapon. It was armour against a single
specific thing: the moment — which

7871
11:02:40,430 --> 11:02:46,585
every dynasty in the history of the galaxy had
eventually met — when eleven billion people

7872
11:02:46,605 --> 11:02:52,553
all become frightened of the same thing on the same
day, and the fear moves faster than

7873
11:02:52,573 --> 11:02:55,161
any instrument of government can move.

7874
11:02:55,730 --> 11:03:01,484
The System had never offered it before. He
understood why it was offering it now, and

7875
11:03:01,504 --> 11:03:07,462
the understanding was not comfortable. The System did
not predict. It priced. And it had

7876
11:03:07,482 --> 11:03:13,576
just put a price on the possibility that the species
would one day look at him and scream.

7877
11:03:14,896 --> 11:03:16,338
Purchase confirmed.

7878
11:03:21,161 --> 11:03:24,516
He went back to the building in twenty
one hundred and forty.

7879
11:03:25,086 --> 11:03:30,860
It was still there. It had been preserved in twenty
sixty-one, over his objection — the

7880
11:03:30,880 --> 11:03:36,854
only public decision of the Directorate that was ever
taken against his stated preference,

7881
11:03:36,874 --> 11:03:42,715
by an Accord Council that voted a hundred and
thirty-nine to two, because eleven billion

7882
11:03:42,735 --> 11:03:47,377
people wanted it and the Council had
learned, by then, when to insist.

7883
11:03:47,947 --> 11:03:54,103
Four storeys of tired brick, on the south bank of
the Christina River, inside a climate

7884
11:03:54,123 --> 11:04:00,351
envelope, in the middle of a white city of nine
million people. The parking lot is still

7885
11:04:00,371 --> 11:04:06,599
a parking lot. The weeds are maintained by a gardener
whose family has held the post for

7886
11:04:06,619 --> 11:04:07,805
four generations.

7887
11:04:08,376 --> 11:04:15,136
The break room is exactly as it was. The vending
machine is a replica; the original is

7888
11:04:15,156 --> 11:04:18,212
in a museum on Mars. The piano is real.

7889
11:04:18,781 --> 11:04:24,717
Four hundred thousand people visit every year. They
queue in the parking lot. They are

7890
11:04:24,737 --> 11:04:28,041
very quiet inside, which nobody
asks them to be.

7891
11:04:30,612 --> 11:04:35,930
He came at night, alone, when it was closed, as
he did every twenty years or so.

7892
11:04:36,499 --> 11:04:42,298
He stood in the break room for a while. Then he sat
down at the piano, which he had never

7893
11:04:42,318 --> 11:04:47,331
once done, in either of his lives, and picked
out four notes with one finger.

7894
11:04:48,901 --> 11:04:53,351
Falling. And falling. And falling. And
landing somewhere unresolved.

7895
11:04:55,921 --> 11:05:01,482
A young woman had played that in this room at three
in the morning in twenty twenty-six,

7896
11:05:01,502 --> 11:05:07,126
and he had asked her why she was there so late, and
she had asked whether she could help,

7897
11:05:07,146 --> 11:05:08,712
and he had said: not yet.

7898
11:05:09,281 --> 11:05:15,147
He played it four times. Then he stopped, and sat with
his hands on the keys, in the dark,

7899
11:05:15,167 --> 11:05:21,098
in a preserved room in a dead building in the middle
of a city that his own will had raised

7900
11:05:21,118 --> 11:05:22,799
out of an industrial park.

7901
11:05:25,367 --> 11:05:27,295
There was nobody to say it to.

7902
11:05:27,864 --> 11:05:33,965
Catherine was in the ground in County Clare. Tomás
was in the ground on the Brandywine.

7903
11:05:33,985 --> 11:05:40,367
Dana, Walter, Lessing, Nadia in exile in Lagos,
Carrick in Portland at ninety-four, Ellery,

7904
11:05:40,387 --> 11:05:46,699
Ingrid Halvorsen, Wen Shulan, who had died at
eighty-eight with her file closed and handed

7905
11:05:46,719 --> 11:05:52,679
on exactly as she had promised. Evelyn was a
hundred and forty billion bodies in nine

7906
11:05:52,699 --> 11:05:56,196
systems and had left him four
words in a notebook.

7907
11:05:56,767 --> 11:06:02,479
And the voice that had argued with him in a thousand
cars had been gone for ninety-three

7908
11:06:02,499 --> 11:06:02,869
years.

7909
11:06:05,940 --> 11:06:11,404
He was the last one. He had built a thing that would
last ten thousand years and he was

7910
11:06:11,424 --> 11:06:15,755
the only person left alive who remembered
the room it had started in.

7911
11:06:37,630 --> 11:06:43,224
Two hundred and seventy-one years later, the
Umbrella Directorate held four hundred and

7912
11:06:43,244 --> 11:06:44,062
nine systems.

7913
11:06:44,632 --> 11:06:50,240
The narrator is going to be brief about those
centuries, because they are not the story,

7914
11:06:50,260 --> 11:06:55,868
and because a great many of them were, in the
ordinary sense, good. Nine hundred billion

7915
11:06:55,888 --> 11:07:01,303
human beings lived across four hundred and nine
worlds. None of them was hungry. None

7916
11:07:01,323 --> 11:07:06,931
of them was at war with another. The average lifespan
was four hundred and eleven years.

7917
11:07:06,951 --> 11:07:12,366
Infant mortality, across the whole of the species,
was a number with nine zeros after

7918
11:07:12,386 --> 11:07:13,517
the decimal point.

7919
11:07:14,089 --> 11:07:19,987
And in two hundred and seventy-one years, no world of
the Directorate ever held an election.

7920
11:07:22,557 --> 11:07:28,052
It was not a tyranny in the way that word was
understood in the twentieth century. There

7921
11:07:28,072 --> 11:07:33,379
were courts, and they were fair. There was law, and
it was applied equally. There was

7922
11:07:33,399 --> 11:07:39,019
speech, and it was not punished, because it did not
need to be. There was no secret police

7923
11:07:39,039 --> 11:07:43,344
on any of the four hundred and nine worlds,
and there never had been.

7924
11:07:43,912 --> 11:07:49,658
There was simply nothing to decide. Every question
that a population might have argued

7925
11:07:49,678 --> 11:07:55,625
about had already been answered, correctly, four
hundred years before, by an intelligence

7926
11:07:55,645 --> 11:08:01,390
that did not age, did not tire, ran nine threads at
four thousand to one, and had been

7927
11:08:01,410 --> 11:08:07,491
right so consistently for so long that disagreement
had become, by about the third century,

7928
11:08:07,511 --> 11:08:11,781
a kind of eccentricity — like insisting
the ground is not solid.

7929
11:08:12,352 --> 11:08:18,226
The Choir's word for it was still on the record.
One note, sustained, by nine hundred

7930
11:08:18,246 --> 11:08:19,335
billion throats.

7931
11:08:22,406 --> 11:08:28,829
He did not change. That is the thing the historians
find hardest, and the biologists hardest

7932
11:08:28,849 --> 11:08:29,320
of all.

7933
11:08:29,889 --> 11:08:35,433
There is no record of Albert Wesker's appearance
altering in four centuries. There is

7934
11:08:35,453 --> 11:08:41,585
no record of his opinions altering either. The man who
stood on the bridge of the Wilmington's

7935
11:08:41,605 --> 11:08:47,214
ninth successor in twenty four hundred and eleven
held, on every substantive question,

7936
11:08:47,234 --> 11:08:53,367
precisely the views he had held in a leather chair in
the rain in September twenty twenty-six.

7937
11:08:53,937 --> 11:08:59,652
He had simply been proved right so many times that
the views had stopped being views and

7938
11:08:59,672 --> 11:09:00,956
become architecture.

7939
11:09:03,525 --> 11:09:09,201
The System still opened when he wanted it. He had not
needed to buy anything in a hundred

7940
11:09:09,221 --> 11:09:14,705
and forty years. The BEYOND tab had eleven more
lines in it, and he had read them, and

7941
11:09:14,725 --> 11:09:20,273
he had been able to afford every one of them for a
century, and he had not bought them,

7942
11:09:20,293 --> 11:09:22,000
and he did not examine why.

7943
11:09:24,820 --> 11:09:28,532
Status. Objectives, none outstanding.

7944
11:09:32,124 --> 11:09:34,484
Objectives: none outstanding.

7945
11:09:35,054 --> 11:09:37,752
It had said that for a hundred
and ninety years.

7946
11:09:40,822 --> 11:09:46,590
They found it four hundred light years beyond the
Serat Reach, in a system with no star.

7947
11:09:47,161 --> 11:09:52,739
It was a structure. It was nine hundred thousand
kilometres across, which is to say that

7948
11:09:52,759 --> 11:09:58,337
it would have contained the orbit of Earth's moon,
and it was made of something that the

7949
11:09:58,357 --> 11:10:03,745
Directorate's instruments could describe but not
explain, and it was dark, and it was

7950
11:10:03,765 --> 11:10:04,953
not doing anything.

7951
11:10:05,524 --> 11:10:11,840
The Veth had a record of it. Their oldest registry,
transcribed from a predecessor civilisation

7952
11:10:11,860 --> 11:10:18,043
that had died before the Hegemony was founded, referred
to it in a phrase that the Hegemony's

7953
11:10:18,063 --> 11:10:24,579
own linguists could only partially render, and which comes
across, in the four human translations,

7954
11:10:24,599 --> 11:10:26,313
as: the one that finished.

7955
11:10:28,885 --> 11:10:31,846
He went himself. Of course he
went himself.

7956
11:10:32,417 --> 11:10:38,297
The structure admitted his ship through an aperture
that opened for it and closed behind

7957
11:10:38,317 --> 11:10:44,533
it, which was the first indication that it was not
dead. Inside, there was air, at a pressure

7958
11:10:44,553 --> 11:10:50,836
and composition that no human had specified, and a
gravity that was not generated by rotation,

7959
11:10:50,856 --> 11:10:56,737
and corridors that were the correct size for a human
being, which they had not been four

7960
11:10:56,757 --> 11:10:57,676
hours earlier.

7961
11:10:58,244 --> 11:11:03,963
He walked for nine hours. He was a hundred and fifty
thousand years too late to meet whatever

7962
11:11:03,983 --> 11:11:08,529
had built it, and he knew that within the
first hour, and he kept walking.

7963
11:11:11,098 --> 11:11:16,806
At the centre there was a chamber, and in the
chamber there was a panel of cold white

7964
11:11:16,826 --> 11:11:19,770
glass, edged in crimson,
hanging in the air.

7965
11:11:24,340 --> 11:11:26,587
He looked at it for a very long time.

7966
11:11:27,157 --> 11:11:32,915
Then he sat down on the floor of the chamber, which he
had not done in four hundred years,

7967
11:11:32,935 --> 11:11:34,328
and read what it said.

7968
11:11:37,646 --> 11:11:49,122
Host terminated. Duration of tenure, one point four
million years. Objectives, none outstanding.

7969
11:11:49,142 --> 11:11:54,031
Host request: cessation. Request granted.

7970
11:11:58,622 --> 11:12:00,615
Somebody else had been given one.

7971
11:12:01,184 --> 11:12:06,912
A hundred and fifty thousand years ago, or four
million, or some number the structure

7972
11:12:06,932 --> 11:12:12,659
did not specify — something had woken up with a
machine in the air that only it could

7973
11:12:12,679 --> 11:12:18,880
see, and had built, and conquered, and won, and gone on
winning for one million four hundred

7974
11:12:18,900 --> 11:12:24,897
thousand years, across nine million systems, until
there was nothing left in the sky that

7975
11:12:24,917 --> 11:12:25,912
it did not own.

7976
11:12:26,482 --> 11:12:29,924
And then it had asked to stop. And the
machine had let it.

7977
11:12:32,994 --> 11:12:36,278
He sat on the floor of that chamber
for nineteen hours.

7978
11:12:36,848 --> 11:12:42,529
There was nobody to say anything to. There had not
been for three hundred years. But he

7979
11:12:42,549 --> 11:12:48,623
found, sitting there, that he was conducting an
argument anyway — that he had been conducting

7980
11:12:48,643 --> 11:12:54,193
it, quietly, in the back of a mind that ran nine
threads, for most of two centuries —

7981
11:12:54,213 --> 11:12:57,862
and that the other side of it had a
voice he recognised.

7982
11:13:00,052 --> 11:13:02,145
Nine million systems.

7983
11:13:02,665 --> 11:13:03,299
Yes.

7984
11:13:03,819 --> 11:13:05,228
And then it stopped.

7985
11:13:05,749 --> 11:13:07,798
It asked to stop. There's a difference.

7986
11:13:08,318 --> 11:13:09,578
Is there?

7987
11:13:12,097 --> 11:13:17,854
It was not the old voice. It had been gone for
three hundred and sixty-four years and

7988
11:13:17,874 --> 11:13:23,630
it was not coming back; the panel had said so in
twenty forty-seven and the panel did

7989
11:13:23,650 --> 11:13:24,174
not lie.

7990
11:13:24,744 --> 11:13:30,739
It was him. It had been him for a very long time.
Somewhere in the fusion — on a balcony

7991
11:13:30,759 --> 11:13:36,549
in Geneva, in the noise of four hundred thousand
people — the two of them had stopped

7992
11:13:36,569 --> 11:13:42,428
being two, and what was left had kept both sets of
arguments, because it had never had

7993
11:13:42,448 --> 11:13:44,137
anything else to talk to.

7994
11:13:46,828 --> 11:13:48,637
We were going to rule all of it.

7995
11:13:49,155 --> 11:13:50,150
We did.

7996
11:13:50,669 --> 11:13:51,397
And then?

7997
11:13:54,417 --> 11:14:00,048
There was no answer, because there had never been
one. That was the whole of it, and it

7998
11:14:00,068 --> 11:14:05,765
had been true in a bunker in nineteen forty-five, and
in a volcano in another world, and

7999
11:14:05,785 --> 11:14:11,547
in a leather chair in the rain in twenty twenty-six,
and on the floor of an empty chamber

8000
11:14:11,567 --> 11:14:15,119
in a starless system in twenty four
hundred and eleven.

8001
11:14:15,689 --> 11:14:21,390
There had never been an after. Not once, in two
lifetimes and four centuries. He had always

8002
11:14:21,410 --> 11:14:26,860
been on the way to something, and the something had
always been more, and now there was

8003
11:14:26,880 --> 11:14:32,392
a panel in front of him that said, in the flat voice
of a machine, that more had an end,

8004
11:14:32,412 --> 11:14:36,605
and that somebody had reached it, and had
not liked what was there.

8005
11:14:40,174 --> 11:14:45,783
He got up, eventually, and walked back to his ship,
and left, and the aperture closed

8006
11:14:45,803 --> 11:14:46,511
behind him.

8007
11:14:47,081 --> 11:14:53,175
He did not destroy the structure. He did not claim
it, or study it, or tell anyone what

8008
11:14:53,195 --> 11:14:59,218
was in it. The Directorate's record of the
expedition runs to four lines and says that

8009
11:14:59,238 --> 11:15:01,537
the object was found to be inert.

8010
11:15:02,106 --> 11:15:08,000
He gave one order on the flight home, to a fleet of
nine hundred vessels, and it is the

8011
11:15:08,020 --> 11:15:12,826
only order in four hundred years that his
officers asked him to repeat.

8012
11:15:15,017 --> 11:15:16,000
We stop here.

8013
11:15:19,019 --> 11:15:24,994
The frontier of the Umbrella Directorate has not moved
since twenty four hundred and eleven.

8014
11:15:27,563 --> 11:15:30,071
He went back to the building
one more time.

8015
11:15:30,640 --> 11:15:35,965
It was four hundred and eighty-five years old by
then, and had been preserved for three

8016
11:15:35,985 --> 11:15:41,310
hundred and twenty of them, and the gardener's
family was in its fourteenth generation.

8017
11:15:41,330 --> 11:15:46,532
The weeds in the parking lot were the descendants
of the weeds that had been there on

8018
11:15:46,552 --> 11:15:50,648
the night a man woke up in a leather chair
with rain on the window.

8019
11:15:51,217 --> 11:15:53,755
He went at night, alone, when
it was closed.

8020
11:15:54,326 --> 11:15:57,163
He sat down at the piano and
opened the lid.

8021
11:15:59,234 --> 11:16:04,411
Four notes. Falling, and falling, and falling,
and landing somewhere unresolved.

8022
11:16:06,980 --> 11:16:12,588
And that is where the narrator is going to leave
him. Not on a bridge, or a balcony, or

8023
11:16:12,608 --> 11:16:18,410
a stage in front of four hundred thousand people. In a
shabby room with a vending machine,

8024
11:16:18,430 --> 11:16:24,296
at a piano that was out of tune when Tomás Reyes made
a joke about it in twenty twenty-six,

8025
11:16:24,316 --> 11:16:29,988
playing four notes that a young woman with nowhere
else to go had played at three in the

8026
11:16:30,008 --> 11:16:33,157
morning, a hundred and
ninety-three years before.

8027
11:16:36,228 --> 11:16:42,053
So. What happened, in the end, when the most
dangerous man of the twentieth century was

8028
11:16:42,073 --> 11:16:48,032
given a second body, a second chance, a machine that
could buy anything, and a world that

8029
11:16:48,052 --> 11:16:49,711
had never heard his name?

8030
11:16:51,782 --> 11:16:52,657
He won.

8031
11:16:53,228 --> 11:16:59,483
That is the answer, and the narrator is not going to
pretend otherwise, and this story

8032
11:16:59,503 --> 11:17:05,832
would be a lie if it ended with him beaten in a
corridor by somebody brave. Nobody beat

8033
11:17:05,852 --> 11:17:12,108
him. Owen Carrick did not beat him, and Nadia Okafor
did not, and Ingrid Halvorsen did

8034
11:17:12,128 --> 11:17:18,749
not, and Wen Shulan did not, and four hundred
intelligence officers and a Norwegian heiress

8035
11:17:18,769 --> 11:17:24,951
and a woman with a jar of bullets did not. He was
faster than all of them, and older,

8036
11:17:24,971 --> 11:17:27,797
and more patient, and he had a machine.

8037
11:17:29,869 --> 11:17:35,758
He ruled the human species for three hundred and
sixty-four years, and under his hand

8038
11:17:35,778 --> 11:17:41,807
it did not starve, and did not fight itself, and
went to the stars, and held a frontier

8039
11:17:41,827 --> 11:17:44,588
against a thing that eats civilisations.

8040
11:17:45,157 --> 11:17:51,511
And it stopped arguing. That is what it cost. Nine
hundred billion people, on four hundred

8041
11:17:51,531 --> 11:17:57,600
and nine worlds, with everything, who had all
quietly agreed — freely, gratefully, one

8042
11:17:57,620 --> 11:18:03,549
reasonable decision at a time, over four centuries
— to let one man do the deciding.

8043
11:18:06,119 --> 11:18:12,372
The Choir was right. They were always right. It is a
silence, wearing the shape of a people,

8044
11:18:12,392 --> 11:18:18,168
and it is beautiful, and it works, and every human
being alive is safer and healthier

8045
11:18:18,188 --> 11:18:22,396
and longer-lived inside it than any
human being has ever been.

8046
11:18:22,965 --> 11:18:26,561
And there has not been a new argument
in four hundred years.

8047
11:18:29,632 --> 11:18:31,753
He taught the stars what a banner is.

8048
11:18:32,322 --> 11:18:36,460
He did it so well that nobody has ever
needed to raise another one.
